hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6013","(6013) Abdă told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to pray four times after that."
"6014","(6014) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza, on the authority of Sharik bin Abi Nimr, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He used to pray four times after that, without making them long."
"6015","(6015) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Asbagh bin Zaid, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Sa’id bin splint; He used to pray four times after that."
"6016","(6016) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Asbagh bin Zaid told us, he said: Thawr bin Zaid told us, about who He told him; On the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: Pray four days after noon, and if you forget the afternoon prayer, it will be there."
"6017","(6017) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He used to pray four times after that."
"6018","(6018) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, who said: Some of Ali’s companions said to Ali: No. Can you tell us about the voluntary prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace during the day? He said: Then Ali said: You will not be able to bear it. He said: So they said: Tell us about it, and we will take from it as much as we can. He said: So he said: When the sun rose from the east, it was as if it had set in the west during the afternoon prayer. He prayed. Two rak'ahs, then if it is from the east as it is from the noon in the west, he prayed four rak'ahs, and he prayed before He prayed four rak'ahs during the noon prayer, two rak'ahs after noon, and prayed four rak'ahs before the afternoon prayer, saying the salutation in each two rak'ahs. Upon the close angels, the prophets, and those who follow them from among the believers and Muslims. (Tirmidhi 424, Ahmad 143)"
"6019","(6019) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Maymun, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: I learned from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, eight rak’ahs; You performed two rak'ahs before noon, two rak'ahs after it, two rak'ahs after sunset, and two rak'ahs after the evening prayer, Hafsiya told me to perform two rak’ahs before dawn. (Tirmidhi 432. Abu Dawud 1246)"
"6020","(6020) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Mughirah ibn Salman, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I preserved from The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed ten rak’ahs, so he mentioned something like the hadith of Ja’far, except that he did not say, “You narrated to me.” Hafsah (Bukhari 1180; Abd al-Razzaq 4811)"
"6021","(6021) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Misra and Zazan, who said: Ali used to pray from Praying four voluntary rak’ahs before noon, two rak’ahs after it, two rak’ahs after sunset, and four after Isha’. And two rak'ahs before dawn."
"6022","(6022) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: Abdullah’s prayer was Which does not detract from voluntary work; Four rak'ahs before noon, two rak'ahs after it, two rak'ahs after sunset, two rak'ahs after Isha', and two rak'ahs Before dawn."
"6023","(6023) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They both said: Voluntary obligatory prayer is ten rak’ahs. You performed two rak'ahs before noon, two rak'ahs after it, two rak'ahs after sunset, and two rak'ahs after the evening prayer, And two rak'ahs before dawn."
"6024","(6024) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to count four of the Sunnahs. before noon, and two rak’ahs after it, and two rak’ahs after sunset, and two rak’ahs after Isha’, and two rak’ahs before Fajr"
"6025","(6025) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abd’s prayer was God whom He does not forsake; Four rak'ahs before noon, two rak'ahs after it, two rak'ahs after sunset, two rak'ahs after Isha', and two rak'ahs Before dawn."
"6026","(6026) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Hilal Al-Wazzan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace, if he missed four prayers before noon, he prayed after them. (Tirmidhi 4261, Ibn Majah 1158)"
"6027","(6027) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of a man from Banu Awud, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: Whoever missed four He prayed before noon prayer after it."
"6028","(6028) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah bin Ziyad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever perseveres in twelve rak’ahs of the Sunnah, God will build for him a house in Paradise. Four rak'ahs before noon, two rak'ahs after it, two rak'ahs after sunset, two rak'ahs after Isha', and two rak'ahs Before dawn. (Tirmidhi 414, Abu Ali 4508)"
"6029","(6029) Yazeed bin Harun told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habiba bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who During the day and night he prayed twelve prostrations in accordance with what is prescribed, and a house was built for him in Paradise. (Tirmidhi 415. Ahmad 6/326)"
"6030","(6030) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Anbasiyah bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan, and she did not narrate it, she said: Whoever prays on the day of twelve days except The written one, a house will be built for him in Paradise."
"6031","(6031) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Ibn Buraidi, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Twelve rak’ahs. Whoever prays it on a day other than what is prescribed will enter Paradise, or a house will be built for him in Paradise. Two rak'ahs before lunch, two rak'ahs after noon, four rak'ahs before noon, two rak'ahs after that, and two rak'ahs after Morocco"
"6032","(6032) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Uthman, the client of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: There is no Muslim servant who prays twelve rak’ahs on a day, except that God builds a house for him in Heaven"
"6033","(6033) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salem, on the authority of Amr bin Aws, On the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habiba, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever prays in... On the twelve day he prostrated voluntarily, a house was built for him in Paradise. (Muslim 503. Abu Dawud 1244)"
"6034","(6034) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ma’rif ibn Wasil, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Whoever prays At the beginning of the day he performed twelve rak'ahs, and a house was built for him in Paradise."
"6035","(6035) Muhammad bin Sulaiman Al-Asbaani told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs on a day, a house will be built for him in Paradise. You bowed before dawn, you bowed before noon, you bowed after noon, and you bowed twice. I think he said: Before the afternoon prayer, and two rak’ahs after sunset, and I think he said: And two rak’ahs after the evening prayer. (Abu Dawud 1263. An-Nasa’i 1481)"
"6036","(6036) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shu’aithi narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anbasa ibn Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habibah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever prays four times before noon, and four After that, God made Hell forbidden to him."
"6037","(6037) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim, he said: When Muadh came, he said: There is no one He prays four voluntary rak'ahs after an obligatory prayer, and on that day no sin will befall him except associating others with God, until he sets. The sun"
"6038","(6038) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Za’ara’; Abu Al-Ahwas did not perform the two rak’ahs before the afternoon prayer."
"6039","(6039) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Al-Hasan used to call the afternoon muezzin to call to prayer, but he would not pray until he had prayed. The afternoon"
"6040","(6040) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, who said: I prayed with the noon judge, then he sat down and did not pray anything. He even prayed the afternoon prayer."
"6041","(6041) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Ismail told me, on the authority of Amer; He was asked about the two rak'ahs before the afternoon prayer? He said: If you know that you will pray it before the iqamah, then pray."
"6042","(6042) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Bishr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He did not pray before the afternoon prayer."
"6043","(6043) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Hafs bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurayh, who said: Hudhayfah was He missed the prayer in his people’s mosque, so he hung up his sandals and followed the mosques until he prayed them in congregation."
"6044","(6044) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad; If he missed the prayer in the mosque of his people, he would go to another mosque."
"6045","(6045) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Abi Rashid, who said: Sa’id ibn Jubayr came to us while we were at the end of Prayer, so he heard a muezzin and came to him."
"6046","(6046) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you miss the prayer in your mosque, do not follow the mosques. Pray in your mosque."
"6047","(6047) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man misses the prayer, The mosque of his people did not follow other mosques."
"6048","(6048) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: He used to miss prayer in a mosque. his people, so he comes to the mosque and enters it, and prays there while he hears the call to prayer from the mosque, but he does not He comes to them."
"6049","(6049) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Al-Sari bin Yahya, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Is there a man who misses prayer in his people’s mosque, so he comes to another mosque? Al-Hasan said: We have not seen the immigrants do that."
"6050","(6050) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar said: He does not pray the same after the prayer."
"6051","(6051) Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musahir, on the authority of Kharsha, he said: Omar hated to pray behind a similar prayer."
"6052","(6052) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Al-Shu’bi, who said: Abdullah said: The funeral prayer should not be prayed upon. After a similar prayer."
"6053","(6053) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Abdullah’s companions, on the authority of Abdullah; He hated to pray something similar to it after the obligatory prayer."
"6054","(6054) Salam Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah hated to He prays the same after the obligatory prayer."
"6055","(6055) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They hated to pray after what was written. For example"
"6056","(6056) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, he said: Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’ told us, he said: They hated to pray after What is written is similar to it."
"6057","(6057) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Suleiman bin Mushir, on the authority of Kharsha bin Al-Hurr, on the authority of Omar; He hated to pray something similar to it after the obligatory prayer."
"6058","(6058) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mihran, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The furthest and furthest from the mosque, the greater the reward. (Abu Dawud 557. Ahmad 2/351)"
"6059","(6059) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Al-Ala’ bin Jariyah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: From the time one of you goes out from his mosque to his house, for one man a good deed is recorded, and for the other You remove evil from him. (Ahmad 2/478, Ibn Hibban 1622)"
"6060","(6060) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Our dwellings were far away. So we wanted to approach the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so we mentioned that to him, and he said: Do not do it. Come as you were. No believer performs ablution and performs it well, then goes out to the mosque, except that God has written He has a good deed in every step, and He has removed from it a bad deed."
"6061","(6061) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Humaid al-Tawil told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik; The people of Salamah wanted to move away from their homes, so they built close to the mosque, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, disliked it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, wanted the city to be stripped bare. He said: O Banu Salama, do you not account for your effects? They said: Yes, so they remained steadfast. (Bukhari 655. Ahmad 3/106)"
"6062","(6062) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; The Banu Salamah had a turn far away from the mosque, so they decided to move closer to the mosque and visit it. Praying with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to them: Don’t you count your effects? Bani Salamah? So they remained steadfast in their homes."
"6063","(6063) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, who said: There was a man in Medina. I do not know of any of the people of Medina who prayed the qiblah farther away from the mosque than him. He was witnessing the prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was said: If you want a donkey, you can ride it in the rain and in the dark. ? He said: By God, I am not pleased that my house is next to the mosque. This was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, just as my sins are written, and my arrival, and my departure, and my return to my family, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: May God grant you that, and give you everything you sought, or as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. And peace be upon him (Muslim 4600, Abu Dawud 558)"
"6064","(6064) Ali bin Hashim told us, he said: I asked Ibn Abi Layla, and I said: Banu Salama wanted to move close to The mosque? It was mentioned on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, with every step you do is good. (Muslim 461)"
"6065","(6065) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: Is any of you unable to move forward when he prays, or He is late, or to his right, or to his left, meaning the Subha. (Abu Dawud 998. Ahmad 2/425)"
"6066","(6066) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He advances, or he delays."
"6067","(6067) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ata’; Ibn Abbas, Ibn al-Zubayr, Abu Sa`id, and Ibn Umar used to say: He does not perform voluntary prayers until he moves from his place. The one in which he prayed the obligatory prayer."
"6068","(6068) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amir, who said: He does not perform voluntary prayers until he has completed his steps, or Two steps"
"6069","(6069) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: When my father prayed the obligatory prayer, he would get down from his place. So he praised you."
"6070","(6070) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Bahr, on the authority of a sheikh, who said: Ibn Masoud was asked about a man who prays in The place where he prayed the obligatory prayer? He said: There is no harm in it."
"6071","(6071) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to pray the Subhaha in his place."
"6072","(6072) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, who said: I saw Al-Qasim and Salem performing the obligatory prayer, then They volunteer in their place. He said: And Nafi’ informed me. Ibn Omar did not see any harm in it."
"6073","(6073) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, who said: I asked Ata’ about a man who volunteers in his place? He said: There is no harm in it."
"6074","(6074) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They were performing the voluntary prayers in the place where they were performing the obligatory prayers."
"6075","(6075) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Other than the imam, if you will. He turns."
"6076","(6076) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Misra, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ali, who said: If the imam greets He did not even volunteer to move from his place, or separate them with words."
"6077","(6077) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He disliked it when the imam prayed to perform a voluntary prayer in his place, and he saw no harm in it for anyone other than the imam."
"6078","(6078) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr; It is disliked for the imam to pray in the place where he prayed the obligatory prayer."
"6079","(6079) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila; It was desirable for the imam, when he prayed, not to perform voluntary prayers in the place in which he prayed. Or he said: He hated it."
"6080","(6080) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan; They were surprised when the Imam came forward."
"6081","(6081) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; It was disliked for the imam to volunteer in the place where he had prayed the obligatory prayer."
"6082","(6082) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Misra, on the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Abbad ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ali, he said: The imam does not volunteer in the place where he led the people until he turns away, or separates with words."
"6083","(6083) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Distawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, who said: The imam turns."
"6084","(6084) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the imam prayed the obligatory prayer, then he wanted to pray it. Voluntary, to step down from the place where he prayed the obligatory prayer."
"6085","(6085) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: They used to like to move forward in prayer, but not They are late."
"6086","(6086) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I said to Muhammad: Does the man advance to the row during prayer? He said: I don't know what's wrong with him taking one or two steps forward. He said to the one arriving in line, objecting: I don’t know what it is?"
"6087","(6087) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who has something and places it down and prays, then he appears to move forward and says: There is no harm in taking it. Then he advances."
"6088","(6088) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, and Sufyan, on the authority of Sa`d bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Urwa, he said: It was said: They came forward, They came forward."
"6089","(6089) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about a man who used to pray while... A people were praying, and they left? He said: He approaches the wall between his hands. He said: I said: Should he recite while walking? He said: No, until he reaches the place where he is standing."
"6090","(6090) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abi Layla, he said: I prayed next to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he voluntarily prayed at night, so he passed by a verse, He said: I seek refuge in God from Hell, and woe to the people of Hell. (Abu Dawud 877. Ahmad 4/347)"
"6091","(6091) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha; She passed by this verse: {So God has bestowed upon us and protected us from the torment of poisons} and said: Oh God, be gracious to us and protect us from the torment of poisons. Indeed, You are the righteous, the merciful. So it was said to Al-Amash: In prayer? He said: In prayer."
"6092","(6092) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Abdul-Wahhab, on the authority of his grandfather, Abbad bin Hamza, who said: I entered On the names of them, and it reads: {So God has bestowed upon us and protected us from the torment of poisons} He said: So she stood on them, and she began to seek refuge and supplicate. Abbad said: So I went to the market and fulfilled my needs, then I came back, and there she was still seeking refuge and praying."
"6093","(6093) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Abdullah said: If one of you mentions the Fire during prayer, Let him seek refuge with God from the Fire, and when he passes by the mention of the Garden, let him ask God about the Garden."
"6094","(6094) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see any harm in asking if he came across a verse, and Ibn Sirin disliked it."
"6095","(6095) Abu Muawiyah and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustarid bin Al-Ahnaf, On the authority of Salah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and whenever he passed by a verse in it was praise. He praised, and when he came across a question he asked, and when he came across a request he sought refuge."
"6096","(6096) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I said to Abraham: I hear the man, while I was praying, saying: {Indeed, God And His angels send blessings upon the Prophet. Shall I pray upon him? He said: Yes, if you wish."
"6097","(6097) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: When a man says in prayer: {Indeed, Allah And His angels send blessings upon the Prophet, O you who have believed, bless him and grant him peace with complete peace}, so may he send blessings upon him. He said: And Ibn Sirin said: When they read the Qur’an, they would not mix with it what was not part of it, and they would go on as they intended."
"6098","(6098) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: I told him: The man passes by these verses in prayer: {Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon the Prophet}. Should he pray upon him? He said: He will pass by."
"6099","(6099) Khaled bin Al-Harith and Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha; A pregnant woman sees blood, but that does not prevent her from praying."
"6100","(6100) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jami’ bin Abi Rashid, on the authority of Ata’; In a pregnant woman you will see blood. He said: Perform ablution and pray."
"6101","(6101) Ismail told us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: I wrote to Nafi’ asking him about a pregnant woman seeing blood? So he wrote to me: I asked Suleiman bin Yassar about a woman seeing blood other than menstruation or postpartum? He said: You wash yourself, cover yourself with a garment, and pray."
"6102","(6102) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, and Ata’; When you are pregnant, you see the blood is dirty, you wash and pray."
"6103","(6103) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; When a pregnant woman sees blood, he said: Do as you would a woman who is experiencing menstruation."
"6104","(6104) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the pregnant woman seeing blood, he said: If she sees it as she saw it before that, then it is in her horoscope; You left the prayer, and if it was only today or two days ago, you did not abandon the prayer."
"6105","(6105) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When she saw him, She is pregnant, so let her perform ablution and pray, for it is nothing."
"6106","(6106) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Al-Hikam; In a pregnant woman you see blood. He said: It is nothing. Hammad said: It is in the same position as the person suffering from istihaadah."
"6107","(6107) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about a pregnant woman seeing blood, Does that prevent her from praying? He said: It is only forbidden from praying and fasting. Menstruation, and this is the end."
"6108","(6108) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, he said: I asked Al-Zuhri about a pregnant woman who sees blood? He said: Stop praying."
"6109","(6109) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Mandal, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Ikrimah, Al-Hakam, and Hammad; They said: Pregnancy and menstruation cannot be combined, so if a pregnant woman sees blood, she should pray."
"6110","(6110) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: If she sees blood on the child, she should stop praying."
"6111","(6111) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; In the mirror she sees blood and she releases it. He said: Do what you would do to a woman who is experiencing menstruation."
"6112","(6112) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim; In a woman who sees blood while she is in labor, he said: It is menstruation, you should not pray."
"6113","(6113) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If she sees blood on a child’s head, she refrains from Prayer"
"6114","(6114) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out to Badr, then he appointed Ibn Umm Maktum as his successor in charge of Medina, and he led them in prayer even though he was blind."
"6115","(6115) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed Ibn Umm Maktum as his successor, and he led the people in prayer even though he was blind. (Abu Dawud 5951. Ahmad 3/192)"
"6116","(6116) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; That some of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to believe while some of them were blind; Itban bin Malik, Muadh bin Afra, and Ibn Umm Maktum."
"6117","(6117) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: There were people from the people of Badr who believed in Their mosques, after their sight had gone."
"6118","(6118) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: We entered upon Jabir bin Abdullah while he was blind. Then the time for prayer came, so he stood up in his weaves, wrapped in them. Whenever he placed them on his shoulders, the two ends of them returned to him. He was young, and his robe was on his side on the holder, so he led us in prayer. (Muslim 147)"
"6119","(6119) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Amer; A man asked Al-Hassan, “Should I lead my people when I am blind?” He said: Yes."
"6120","(6120) Ruh bin Ubadah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about the blind man leading in prayer? He said: Then he said: If he is the most learned of them."
"6121","(6121) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm for a blind person to lead in prayer."
"6122","(6122) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Muhajir, who said: Al-Bara’ used to lead us in prayer even though he was blind."
"6123","(6123) Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Abbas is blind."
"6124","(6124) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of Ibn Lamīr, on the authority of his father; That a blind man used to lead Banu Khatima in prayer during the time of my life."
"6125","(6125) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Rabi’, on the authority of Itban bin Malik; He used to lead his people in prayer even though he was blind."
"6126","(6126) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Anas narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Itban bin Malik; He used to lead his people in prayer even though he was blind. (Bukhari 667, An-Nasa’i 863)"
"6127","(6127) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, he said: The imam of Banu Khatmiya was blind."
"6128","(6128) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: Jabir made us safe after he had gone. His sight"
"6129","(6129) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: Al-Hakam bin Utaybah asked Al-Qasim about the blind man. He leads, and is his testimony permissible? He said: What prevents him from leading and his testimony being accepted?"
"6130","(6130) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Omar Ibn Atiyya, who said: Al-Musayyab believed us while he was blind."
"6131","(6131) Al-Fadl bin Dukain told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of a sheikh whose nickname is Abu Abdullah; Verily, my father’s son fulfilled his mother’s faith even though he was blind."
"6132","(6132) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: How? My followers and they will turn me towards the qiblah."
"6133","(6133) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Abi Al-Hasana’i, on the authority of Ziyad Al-Numayri, he said: I asked Anas about The blind man, should he lead the prayer? He said: Who is the poorest of you in that?"
"6134","(6134) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Wasil al-Ahdab, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Burmah al-Asadi, he said: Abdullah: I do not like your muezzins to be your blind men. He said: I think so. He said: Nor do your readers."
"6135","(6135) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Marzuq, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, that he said: The blind man does not He leads"
"6136","(6136) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man from Tay; Ibn Masoud performed Hajj and prayed behind a Bedouin."
"6137","(6137) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Al-Abbas Al-Jariri; That Abu Majliz hated the Bedouin imam, and that Al-Hasan did not see anything wrong with that."
"6138","(6138) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Darim, who said: I asked Salim: Do Bedouins lead migrants? He said: And what do you have to do if he is a righteous man?"
"6139","(6139) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; That he was asked about the imamate of a slave and a Bedouin? He said: When the servant understands it, he loves them to me."
"6140","(6140) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm for a Bedouin to lead in prayer."
"6141","(6141) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; Ibn Masoud prayed behind a Bedouin."
"6142","(6142) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Burd Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: There were imams of That work, meaning children of adultery."
"6143","(6143) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the child of adultery being the one to lead the prayer."
"6144","(6144) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Zuhair bin Abi Thabit Al-Absi, he said: I heard Al-Sha’bi, He says: His testimony is permissible, and he leads."
"6145","(6145) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He was asked about the imam of the child of adultery? He said: We have an imam whose father is not known."
"6146","(6146) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the child of fornication leading in prayer."
"6147","(6147) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Hanifa told us, he said: I asked Ata’ about the child of fornication. Should he lead the people in prayer? He said: There is no harm in it. Is there not one of them who fasts and prays more than us?"
"6148","(6148) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in the child of adultery being the one to lead the prayer."
"6149","(6149) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The child of fornication and others alike."
"6150","(6150) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn al-Mundhir al-Thawri, who said: I asked al-Harith al-Ukli about the child of adultery. Is he leading? He said: Yes."
"6151","(6151) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; What if she was asked about the child of adultery? She said: He does not have any sin on his parents. Do not bear the burden of another woman’s burden."
"6152","(6152) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: I have heard that Omar bin Abdul-Aziz said to a man, He was leading some people in prayer with the aqeeq, and he did not know who his children were, so he forbade him to lead them in prayer."
"6153","(6153) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; He hated to lead a child born of adultery and a gossiper."
"6154","(6154) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Dawud bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Yahya al-Mazni narrated to me; That a man was punished for committing a crime, and he was leading his companions in prayer, so they asked Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and he said: How did you see him? They said: He was as he was, so they praised him well, so he ordered him to lead them."
"6155","(6155) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Imran al-Juniy, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Dharr ; He came and Ali al-Rabadha was an Ethiopian slave, so the prayer was performed, and he said: Come forward."
"6156","(6156) Yazid told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; That Abu Dharr came as a slave."
"6157","(6157) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Dharr; He prayed behind an Ethiopian slave."
"6158","(6158) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Malika, on the authority of Aisha; Indeed, her mother was taking care of her."
"6159","(6159) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father; Aisha prayed behind a mamluk of hers."
"6160","(6160) Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, the servant of my father Asid said: I got married while I was a slave, so I invited some of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Abu Dharr, Ibn Masoud, and Hudhayf, then the prayer was established, and Abu Dharr came forward and said: Behind you, so he turned to his companions. He said: Is that so? He said: Yes, he said: They brought me forward, and I prayed with them while I was a slave slave."
"6161","(6161) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Dawud bin al-Husayn, on the authority of Abi Sufyan; He used to lead Banu Abd al-Ashhal, who were in offices, and among them were men from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Muhammad bin Muslima and Salamah bin Salamah, so they wanted to delay it, so when they heard it being read, they said: Is this something that would be delayed?"
"6162","(6162) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, who said: There is no harm for a servant to lead in prayer."
"6163","(6163) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Indeed, he did not see any harm in the servant being led in prayer."
"6164","(6164) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no harm for a servant to lead in prayer."
"6165","(6165) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shehr, who said: There is no harm for a servant to lead in prayer if he is the most knowledgeable among them."
"6166","(6166) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Ziyad, the client of Umm al-Hasan, who said: Salem bin Abdullah prayed behind me, and I was a servant."
"6167","(6167) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Al-Abbas Al-Jariri; That Abu Majliz hated the servant’s imam, and that Al-Hasan did not see any harm in him."
"6168","(6168) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, saying: Ibn Juraij informed me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubad Allah bin Abi Your kingdom; They were coming to Aisha, her father, Ubaid bin Umair, Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, and many people. Then Abu Amr, a servant of Aisha, led them in prayer, and Abu Amr at that time was a boy who had not been freed."
"6169","(6169) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: This servant used to lead in prayer in our mosque. For forty years, a mosque where a group of people used to pray."
"6170","(6170) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Bashar bin Kadam Al-Salami, on the authority of Amr bin Misra, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali; He prayed behind a slave in one of his walls, and people from his household."
"6171","(6171) Waki’ told us, he said: Bashir bin Salman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Bastam Al-Tamimi, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: No. The slaves will lead in prayer, and among them there will be a free person, and he who has not performed Hajj will not lead in prayer, and among them will be those who have performed Hajj."
"6172","(6172) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim bin Abi Habib narrated to me, he said: Abdullah bin Abi narrated to me. Sufyan, on the authority of his father, said: I went out with Abdullah bin Jaafar, Hussein bin Ali, and Ibn Abi Ahmad to Yanbu. So I attended the prayer, and they brought me forward, so I prayed with them."
"6173","(6173) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Sulaiman bin al-Ghasil narrated to us, saying: Al-Mundhir bin Abi narrated to me. Usayd Al-Ansari said: My father was praying behind me, so he might have said to me: O my son, you have spent a long time with us today."
"6174","(6174) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Yazid al-Makki told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: The man does not lead in prayer. His father"
"6175","(6175) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Aban bin Yazid Al-Attar narrated to us, on the authority of Badil bin Misra Al-Uqaili, on the authority of Abu Atiyya, one of them, said: Malik bin Al-Huwarith used to come to our place of prayer and we would talk. Prayer, so we said to him: Come forward, and he said: No, let some of you come forward so that I may tell you why I do not come forward. I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, says: Whoever visits a people should not lead them, and a man from among them should lead them. (Abu Dawud 5961. Ahmad 3/436)"
"6176","(6176) Jarir and Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Simak bin Salma al-Dhabi, who said: I saw Ibn Omar and Ibn Abbas. And they were standing square in prayer."
"6177","(6177) Hafs told us, on the authority of Uqabi, he said: I saw a man praying cross-legged."
"6178","(6178) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Ubaid al-Tai, on the authority of his brother, who said: I saw a person praying cross-legged."
"6179","(6179) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Omar Al-Ansari, he said: I saw a man praying, cross-legged on his head."
"6180","(6180) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jahadi, who said: I saw Salim praying cross-legged."
"6181","(6181) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raja’, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He prays cross-legged."
"6182","(6182) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: I saw Abu Bakr praying, cross-legged and reclining."
"6183","(6183) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, who said: I saw Ata’ praying cross-legged."
"6184","(6184) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, saying: I saw Ibn Sirin praying cross-legged."
"6185","(6185) Ubaidullah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar; He used to sit cross-legged during prayer."
"6186","(6186) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Dulham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in praying the voluntary prayers while sitting cross-legged."
"6187","(6187) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Haytham bin Shihab; He saw a man from his people praying, sitting cross-legged, so he stopped him, but he refused to obey him, so Al-Haytham said: I heard Abdullah bin Masoud say: It is more beloved to me to sit on my knees than to sit cross-legged during prayer."
"6188","(6188) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, he said: I asked the ruling about squatting in prayer? It is as if he hated it. He said: And I think he said: Ibn Abbas hated it."
"6189","(6189) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; He disliked praying cross-legged, and he said: Sit other than your usual sitting position for the hadith."
"6190","(6190) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim; He disliked sitting in prayer like a man talking to his friends."
"6191","(6191) Waki’ told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Hakim Al-San’ani, he said: I saw Ibn Umar Cross-legged during the last prayer, when he raised his head from the last prostration. When he prayed, I said to him? He said: I feel pain in my leg."
"6192","(6192) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’; Ibn Umar prayed cross-legged due to pain."
"6193","(6193) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: It was disliked for a man to sit crouched down in his prayer until He is witnessing."
"6194","(6194) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; I was informed that Ibn Umar prayed cross-legged, and said: It is not a Sunnah. I only do it as a result of pain."
"6195","(6195) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; He disliked sitting cross-legged, and said: Sitting is your kingdom."
"6196","(6196) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When he prays sitting, he makes himself standing. squared"
"6197","(6197) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Sulayman bin Bazi’, who said: I entered upon Salem while he was praying sitting. When sitting, he bows his knees, and when standing, he bows cross-legged."
"6198","(6198) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan said: If he prays sitting, he makes his standing cross-legged, and if he wants to kneel, he kneels. He is cross-legged, so when he wants to prostrate, he bends his legs."
"6199","(6199) Waki’ told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: When he prays Cross-legged, Mas’ar said: Or as he said, he sits, so if he wants to bow, or prostrate, he bends his legs."
"6200","(6200) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: He prays cross-legged, so if he wants To kneel with his legs bent."
"6201","(6201) Waki’ told us, he said: Hassan told us, on the authority of Abu Hafs, he said: I saw a man praying cross-legged, so if he wanted to He kneels with his legs bent."
"6202","(6202) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man entering the mosque after the line had been completed. He said: If he is able to enter the line, he will do so. If not, he takes a man’s hand and makes him stay in line. With him, and he did not rise alone."
"6203","(6203) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, who said: I said to Ibrahim: Should I come to the class when it is full? He said: Pass by a man, and let him stay with you. If you pray alone, then repeat."
"6204","(6204) Abu Muawiyah and Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; He used to lead his wives in prayer during the prescribed period, and there was no man with them."
"6205","(6205) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar ibn al-Khattab made people recite in Ramadan. Ubayy used to lead the people in prayer, and Ibn Abi Hatthama led the women in prayer."
"6206","(6206) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ghalib Abi al-Hudhayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I was praying in Alive at the time of al-Hajjaj, and there is only a woman behind me."
"6207","(6207) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi and Ata’ about a man who leads women in prayer, not Is there a man with them? They said: There is no harm in it."
"6208","(6208) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Abdullah Al-Thaqafi, he said: Arfajah narrated to us, he said: It was Ali. He commanded the people to observe Ramadan, and he used to appoint an imam for the men and an imam for the women. Arfaja said: Then Ali appointed me as the imam of the women."
"6209","(6209) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He was asked about a man who leads women in prayer during Ramadan? He said: He saw no harm in it if the man was there. There is no harm in it. He said: And if the man were to go out, then he would miss the prayer. A group, so he returns to his family, gathers them, and prays with them."
"6210","(6210) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Mutayr ibn Juwayriyah, who said: I saw Abu Majliz and he had a mosque in his house. Perhaps he gathered with his family and boys."
"6211","(6211) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Naim, who said: Omar said: If there is a path between him and the Imam, Or a river, or a wall, it is not with it."
"6212","(6212) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated to lead the imam’s prayer if there was a road between them, or women."
"6213","(6213) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Ezzah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I asked him about The woman follows the imam, and is there a way between them? He said: That is not for her."
"6214","(6214) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: Anas was gathering prayers with the imam, and he was in the house of Nafi’ ibn Abd al-Harith. A house overlooking the mosque, with a door to the mosque, so he used to gather in it and follow the imam."
"6215","(6215) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Salih, the client of the twins, who said: I prayed with Abu Hurairah. Above the mosque with the imam’s prayer, while he is below."
"6216","(6216) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Majliz; In a woman praying, and between her and the imam there is a wall. He said: If she hears the takbeer, that is sufficient for her."
"6217","(6217) Abu Amer Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Muslim, who said: I saw Salem bin Abdullah praying on the back of his head. The mosque is the Maghrib prayer, and there is another man with him, who takes care of and follows the imam."
"6218","(6218) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: There was a roof next to our mosque, to the right of the mosque, lower than The Imam, and there were people fleeing from the command of the pilgrims, and between them and the mosque there was a long wall, and they were praying over that. roof, and they follow the imam, so I mentioned it to Abraham, and he thought it was good."
"6219","(6219) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad was asked about a man who was on the outside of a house. He prays with the imam’s prayer in Ramadan? He said: I do not know of any harm in it, unless it is in the hands of the Imam."
"6220","(6220) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa; That Urwa was praying with the prayer of the imam, and he was in the house of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith, and between them and The mosque is on the road."
"6221","(6221) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He was asked about the muezzin standing in the minaret. And he prays with the imam’s prayer? He said: It is sufficient."
"6222","(6222) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about the muezzin’s prayer. Above the mosque on Friday with the imam praying while he was down? He said: That will suffice for them."
"6223","(6223) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about the muezzin praying in his cell. And he follows the imam? He thought that"
"6224","(6224) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman al-Taimiyi, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Omar said: A woman prays in three garments."
"6225","(6225) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Aisha was asked: How long does a woman pray? She said: Go to Ali and ask him, then return to me. So he came to Ali and asked him, and he said: In bright armor and a veil, so he returned to her. So he told her, and she said: He told the truth."
"6226","(6226) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Bukair bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Ubad Allah Al-Khawlani, he said: I saw Maimunah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying in a single piece of armor, and she had put some of her sleeves on it. Her head. He said: `Ubaidullah was an orphan in her care."
"6227","(6227) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Anas narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Ubaid Allah Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Maimunah bint Al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; She prayed wearing armor and a veil."
"6228","(6228) Hafs told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zaid, who said: My mother told me; She asked Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: What should a woman pray about? She said: She prays in a thick shield that covers her feet and the veil."
"6229","(6229) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Saad informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zayd bin Muhajir bin Qunfud, on the authority of his mother, On the authority of Umm Salama, she said: A woman prays in bright armor and a veil."
"6230","(6230) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Umm Thawr, on the authority of her husband Bishr; He asked Ibn Abbas: How much should a woman pray? He said: In armor and a veil."
"6231","(6231) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: If a woman prays, Let her pray fully clothed; The armor, the veil, and the veil."
"6232","(6232) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah, who said: A woman prays in armor and a veil. And the loins\n Ash'ath said, on the authority of Muhammad, the same, so I said to him: What is this wine? He said: The veil is that which is covered with veil, and the Ansar used to call the loincloth the loincloth."
"6233","(6233) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: A woman prays in three dresses."
"6234","(6234) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Hilal told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: It was desirable for a woman to pray. In three dresses: In the armor, the veil, and the loins."
"6235","(6235) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to permit women to pray in armor and robes."
"6236","(6236) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: A woman said to my father: A woman is pregnant, and he It is difficult for me to pray in plain clothes, so should I pray in armor and a veil? He said: Yes."
"6237","(6237) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A woman prays in a discreet armor and veil."
"6238","(6238) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: A woman prays in Solid armor, and solid veil."
"6239","(6239) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Ata’ said: In armor and a veil."
"6240","(6240) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked the arbitrator, and he said: In armor and a veil, and I asked Hammad, and he said: You pray in A shield and a veil covering her head."
"6241","(6241) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A woman should not pray wearing less than four garments."
"6242","(6242) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Mu’adh, on the authority of Aisha; She stood praying in armor and a veil, and the mother came to her and threw a garment over her."
"6243","(6243) Azhar Al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Girdle yourself with it."
"6244","(6244) Ibn Fadil told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, who said: I asked Mujahid and Ata’ about a woman attending the prayer. And she only has one garment? They said: You should wear it."
"6245","(6245) Waki’ told us, he said: Omar bin Dhar told us, he said: I asked Ata’ about a woman who wears nothing but a garment. The one? He said: You should cover yourself with it.\n Waki` said: It means if he is young."
"6246","(6246) Waki’ told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir; He led them in one shirt."
"6247","(6247) Waki’ told us, he said: Aban bin Sam’a told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no harm in prayer. In one shirt, if it is thin."
"6248","(6248) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail al-Sarraj, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He prayed in a shirt with nothing else on it."
"6249","(6249) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Salih, on the authority of Musa ibn Yazid, who said: I heard Abu Imamah say: He was asked about praying wearing one shirt? He said: There is no harm in it. And what about the bond? If you cover yourself with it, there is no problem with it."
"6250","(6250) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, he said: Ibn Abbas was asked about prayer in One shirt? He said: O Lord, there is a man who has nothing but a shirt."
"6251","(6251) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in praying in one shirt if it is Cheeky"
"6252","(6252) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, he said: Mu’awiyah believed in him. Shirt"
"6253","(6253) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman; He prayed in a shirt."
"6254","(6254) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hind, who said: I sent a boy as a scribe to me. Asking Saeed bin Al-Musayyab about praying in a shirt with no garment underneath it? He said: There is nothing wrong with him if he is not healed."
"6255","(6255) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Ikrimah; He did not see any harm in praying in one prudent shirt."
"6256","(6256) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dhail bin Bilal Al-Fazari, he said: Ziyad bin Othman Al-Ahmari narrated to me, He said: I saw Alqamiya praying in a short, thick shirt."
"6257","(6257) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, he said: There is no harm in praying in one garment. If he is honest."
"6258","(6258) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Israel Ismail told us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Amr, he said: There is no harm in prayer In one shirt if it is thin."
"6259","(6259) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: Al-Hakam prayed in a thick shirt, and Al-Hakam said: There is no harm in praying in it. One shirt if it is thin."
"6260","(6260) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Layya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Nawfal, he said: I saw Urwa Ibn Al-Zubayr prays in a shirt, nothing else is on him."
"6261","(6261) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, who said: Jabir bin Zayd was asked about the man. Does he pray wearing a single forehead, or a thick shirt, and his private parts are covered, and there is nothing else on him? He said: There is no harm in it."
"6262","(6262) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: Malika bint Abi Abd al-Rahman narrated to me; Her father used to pray voluntarily in a shirt at night."
"6263","(6263) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam; That Saad led the people in prayer in a watering hole."
"6264","(6264) Waki’ told us, he said: Aban bin Sam’a told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no harm in prayer. In one forehead."
"6265","(6265) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Za’id bin Qadamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid bin Jud’an, he said: I asked Sa’id Ibn Al-Musayyab about praying in the forehead? He said: And in the shirt if it is thick."
"6266","(6266) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Rabi’ bin Subayh informed us, he said: Tell me who saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz. He prays wearing a long garment, wearing no garment."
"6267","(6267) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhall, who said: I saw Abraham praying in a place of water, without putting out his hand. From us"
"6268","(6268) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If any woman prays and does not cover her hair, she will not May her prayers be accepted."
"6269","(6269) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who narrated it, saying: If a slave girl menstruates, it will not be accepted for her. Prayer except with a veil. (Tirmidhi 3771, Abu Dawud 641)"
"6270","(6270) Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father; He sent a woman to Aisha, and she saw her maid with a whole family, and she said: If she had covered herself, it would have been better. She said: She did not menstruate, nor did it start after menstruation."
"6271","(6271) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad; On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me while there was a young woman with me, and he threw his loins toward me and said: There is a difference between this girl and the one at?? Umm Salama, I do not see her unless she has menstruated. (Abu Dawud 642. Ahmad 6/238)"
"6272","(6272) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon her, and she hid as a servant of theirs. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Did she menstruate? They said: Yes, so he cut part of his turban for her and said: Cover it with this. (Ibn Majah 654)"
"6273","(6273) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Mahan, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: When she menstruates The slave girl is obligated to cover up as it is obligatory for her mother."
"6274","(6274) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Marzuq bin Abdullah, the client of Banu Zuhara, narrated to us, saying: I asked Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab: When is the prayer prescribed for a slave girl? He said: If she menstruates."
"6275","(6275) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If a slave girl menstruates, it is obligatory She must cover up as much as her mother is obligated to."
"6276","(6276) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Rabi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If a slave girl menstruates, her prayer will not be accepted unless With a veil"
"6277","(6277) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If a slave girl menstruates, it will not be accepted. There is no prayer except with a veil."
"6278","(6278) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Salem, who said: Aisha said: When she had a wet dream The slave woman is obligated to do what is obligatory upon her mother. It means from concealment."
"6279","(6279) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Safiyya, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God will not accept the prayer of a menstruating woman unless she is wearing a veil."
"6280","(6280) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a woman reaches the age of menstruation and does not cover her ears And her head, her prayer was not accepted."
"6281","(6281) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: You pray as you go out."
"6282","(6282) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq; Ali and Shurayh used to say: A mother prays as she leaves."
"6283","(6283) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The mother of the child prays without a veil, even if she has reached puberty. Sixty years"
"6284","(6284) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: A slave woman is not required to wear a veil, even if She was old."
"6285","(6285) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: There is no veil on the slave women."
"6286","(6286) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The slave woman prays as she leaves."
"6287","(6287) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith, he said: The mother prays as she leaves."
"6288","(6288) Abd al-Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: The slave woman prays as she leaves."
"6289","(6289) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: A mother is not required to wear a veil, even if she gives birth to Her master"
"6290","(6290) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “The mother has shed her scalp.”"
"6291","(6291) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, he said: Omar saw a mother of ours wearing a mask. So he hit her and said: Do not resemble silk women."
"6292","(6292) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Omar said: The mother has cast She saw her head from behind the wall."
"6293","(6293) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khaled Al-Makhzoumi, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, with a similar hadith Waki', on the authority of his people, on the authority of the government."
"6294","(6294) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, who said: Umar saw a masked slave girl, so he hit her. And he said: Do not resemble silk women."
"6295","(6295) Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Falfil, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: She entered upon Omar bin Al-Khattab. His mother was introducing her to some of the Muhajirin or Ansar, and she was wearing a robe, wearing it, so they asked her: Was she emancipated? She said: No, he said: What about the jilbab? Place it on your head. The jilbab is only worn by the freed women of the believers. She hesitated, so he went up to her with the cloak and struck it. With her head until she threw it off her head."
"6296","(6296) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Abu Hubaira asked him: How do female slaves pray? He said: You pray as you go out."
"6297","(6297) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, who said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab did not leave a mother in his caliphate. disguise yourself He said: And Omar said: The mask is for the silkies, so that they do not harm them."
"6298","(6298) Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, he said: A worker came to Muawiyah, and he sent him to collect alms, so he stayed a house. So when he came to two mosques, he said: Which one is the first? So he was informed about it, and the one who was the oldest of them came."
"6299","(6299) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Laith; That Abu Wael missed the prayer in such-and-such mosque, so he prayed in such-and-such mosque, and between them there were mosques. Many of them were newly invented, he did not pray on them."
"6300","(6300) Mu’tamir ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Amara al-Saydalani, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, who said: I used to be with Anas. So he comes to the mosque and hears the call to prayer, and says: Is this new? If they say: Yes, then move on to something else."
"6301","(6301) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; It was going beyond the modern mosques to the ancient ones."
"6302","(6302) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Awf, he said: A man from the people of the desert told me, he said: A confirmer from Medina, the nights of Muawiyah. While he was at a water station for us one day, he said: And the prayer came, and at the water Two of the mosques of the people of the desert. He said: Which one was built first? It was said: This, so he meant something like it."
"6303","(6303) Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a man who left his people’s mosque and came to another one? He said: Al-Hasan said: They loved for a man to increase his people by himself."
"6304","(6304) Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father; That Omar entered the mosque and bowed in it once, and they said to him? He said: It is voluntary, so whoever wishes can increase, and whoever wants can decrease."
"6305","(6305) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qaboos bin Abi Dhabyan, on the authority of his father; Omar ibn al-Khattab passed by the mosque and bowed one rak’ah, and it was said to him: Did you only kneel once? He said: It is voluntary, and I hate to take it as a way."
"6306","(6306) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, he said: He narrated to me someone who saw Talhah ibn Ubaid Allah passing through the mosque and bowing down. Then he left."
"6307","(6307) Waki’ told us, he said: A partner told us, on the authority of Simak, he said: He told us who saw Talha ibn Ubaidullah passing by. The mosque, so he prostrated prostratingly."
"6308","(6308) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Saif bin Misra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: I saw Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam come out of Palace, then he passed by the mosque and bowed, or prostrated."
"6309","(6309) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, on the authority of Rashid ibn Saad, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace They pray, may God bless him and grant him peace, and upon them is their punishment."
"6310","(6310) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas bin Hakim, he said: Rashid bin Saad narrated to me, on the authority of Urwah bin Al-Zubayr, he said It used to be said: Swords are the weapons of invaders."
"6311","(6311) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They believed that swords In the same position as a robe during prayer."
"6312","(6312) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The sword is in the same position as the robe in prayer."
"6313","(6313) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, who said: I saw Ibrahim The Taymiyyah prays with no robe on him except his sword."
"6314","(6314) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, saying: They were the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. They pray on swords, with kilts made of the skin of the dead on them."
"6315","(6315) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Swords are the weapons of the invaders."
"6316","(6316) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The bow does not suffice in place of a robe."
"6317","(6317) Hushaym told us, he said: `Ubaidah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: The bow is in the place of the robe."
"6318","(6318) Uqba bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Musa bin Muhammad bin Ibrahim, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Salma bin The elbows; That he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about praying with the bow and the horn? He said: Pray in the bow, and cast the horn. (Abu Ali 379)"
"6319","(6319) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: It was when it was night. It was rainy, or very windy. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded a caller and he called out: “Pray in your lodgings.” (Bukhari 6661, Muslim 484)"
"6320","(6320) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of his father, he said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. In the year of Hudaybiyyah or Hunayn, we were greeted with rain that did not wet the soles of our sandals, so the herald of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called out. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: To pray in your travels. (Abu Dawud 1050, Ahmad 5/75)"
"6321","(6321) Hushaym told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Abu Raja’, he said: We were struck by rain on the day of Friday in At the time of Ibn Abbas, he ordered a caller and he called out: Pray in your camps."
"6322","(6322) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, he said: I went out one night I went to the mosque, and when I came back I opened the door. My father said: Who is this? They said: Abu Al-Malih. He said: You saw us with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Al-Hudaybiyyah, and we were struck. The sky did not wet the soles of our sandals, so the herald of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called out: “Pray in your saddles.”"
"6323","(6323) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of his commanders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samarra; The day of Hunayn was a rainy day, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded his caller: Prayer is to be performed while traveling. (Bukhari 615. Ahmad 5/74)"
"6324","(6324) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Our princes were when the night came. When it was raining, they delayed Maghrib and hastened for Isha before twilight had set. Ibn Umar was praying with them without being seen. That's a big deal. Ubaidullah said: I saw Al-Qasim and Salim praying with them on a night like that."
"6325","(6325) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, who said: I saw Saeed bin al-Musayyab praying with When the imams gather between Maghrib and Isha on a rainy night."
"6326","(6326) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, who said: I saw Aban bin Othman He combines the two prayers on a rainy night. Maghrib and evening prayers, and Urwah bin Al-Zubayr, Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Abu Bakr bin Abdul-Rahman will pray with him. And Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, they do not deny him."
"6327","(6327) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Abu Maudud Abdul Aziz bin Abi Suleiman, who said: I prayed with Abu Bakr. Ibn Muhammad attended the Maghrib and the evening prayers, so he brought them together on a rainy night."
"6328","(6328) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar was praying with Marwan, and he Marwan: If it was a rainy night, he combined Maghrib and Isha’, and Ibn Umar used to pray both with him."
"6329","(6329) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Anas informed me, on the authority of Dawud bin Husayn, he said: An informant informed me. On the authority of Ibn Abbas; In His saying, Blessed and Most High: {For the setting of the sun} He said: When the Fay’ is complete. {By the night and what it gave rise to} He said: and what it combined."
"6330","(6330) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: {the setting of the sun} After midday."
"6331","(6331) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “Establish the prayer when the sun sets.” Until the dusk of the night} He said: its setting."
"6332","(6332) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Nafi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father: {Establish the prayer at the setting of the sun} He said: its setting before it sets."
"6333","(6333) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Ismail bin Abdul-Malik narrated to us, he said: Yunus bin Khabab narrated to me, On the authority of Mujahid, he said: I was leading my master al-Sa’ib, who was blind, and he said to me: O Mujahid, has the sun made you shine? If I said yes, he stood up and prayed the noon prayer."
"6334","(6334) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, he said: I was sitting With Abdullah in his house, when the sun set, so Abdullah said: {Establish the prayer from the setting of the sun until dusk of the night} Then he said: This is by God, besides Whom there is no god, when the fasting person breaks his fast and the time for this prayer has arrived."
"6335","(6335) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid ibn Jaafar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Its buckets are full."
"6336","(6336) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Ya’qub al-Qummi, on the authority of Ja’far bin Abi al-Mughirah, who said: Its disappearance"
"6337","(6337) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Kudayna, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Its disappearance"
"6338","(6338) Shababih told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The setting of the sun until it sets, And the dusk of the night is the setting of the sun."
"6339","(6339) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Umays narrated to us, saying: He narrated to me and he was innocent, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah and Ibn Abbas said: Its bucket when it sets."
"6340","(6340) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ali, who said: Its descent is its sunset."
"6341","(6341) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He said: Ubayd Allah ibn Utbah’s eyesight was gone, so the doctor came and said: I will treat you on the condition that you lie down for seven days, and no You pray unless lying down, but he refused and hated it."
"6342","(6342) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wa’il; Water fell into his eyes, and he was told: “Lie down for seven days,” so he decided to do so."
"6343","(6343) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: When his sight stopped, he came to him. A man, and he said to him: If you are patient with me for seven days and do not pray except lying down, I will treat you, and I hope that your eye will be healed. He said: Ibn Abbas sent to Aisha, Abu Hurairah, and other of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: They all say: Have you seen that if you die on these seven days, what will you do with prayer? He said: He left his eyes, but they did not treat them."
"6344","(6344) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha; Ibn Abbas had water thrown into his eyes, and it was said to him: Do you lie down for seven days, and only pray lying down? So he sent to Aisha and Umm Salama, and he asked them, but they refused."
"6345","(6345) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar, he said: If it is a cloudy day, hasten the afternoon and delay the noon."
"6346","(6346) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Hasten the daytime prayer on a cloudy day, and delay the Maghrib prayer."
"6347","(6347) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Hazzam bin Jabir, he said: I heard Ibn Masoud, He says: When it is a cloudy day, hasten the noon prayer, delay the afternoon prayer, and delay the sunset prayer."
"6348","(6348) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Awza’i narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abi Qalabi, on the authority of Abi Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Buraida Al-Aslami, said: We were with him on his campaign, and he said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: Arrive early to pray on a cloudy day, for whoever misses the afternoon prayer, his work has been vain. (Ibn Majah 694, Ahmad 361)"
"6349","(6349) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham al-Dastawwi told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Qalab, On the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Buraidah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a similar manner. (Bukhari 594. Ahmad 5/439)"
"6350","(6350) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Bakr bin Ma’iz, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym, He said to the muezzin: If it is a cloudy day, then set at sunset."
"6351","(6351) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It was a wonder for him, on a cloudy day, to delay Dhuhr, and hastens the afternoon."
"6352","(6352) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, who said: The afternoon is hastened by a cloudy day. Maghrib is delayed."
"6353","(6353) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He hastens the afternoon and delays it. Morocco"
"6354","(6354) Yahya bin Yaman narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, with something similar."
"6355","(6355) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah; (They were not hungry during the night) He said: They do not sleep for the after-evening night."
"6356","(6356) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan; {They were not hungry for a little while of the night, and at dawn they sought forgiveness.} He said: They prayed, but when dawn came they asked forgiveness."
"6357","(6357) Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rawahih; {They were hungry for a little while of the night} He said: They were hungry for a little while, then they extended it until dawn."
"6358","(6358) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; {They were not relieved for a little of the night}. He said: That was when they were commanded to pray the night prayers, and Abu Dharr was detained. He detained him, and he took the stick and leaned on it, and they were like that until the concessions came down: {So recite what is possible. From Him}"
"6359","(6359) Affan narrated to us, he said: Bukair bin Abi Al-Sumait narrated to us, he said: His leaders narrated to us; In the words of God Almighty: {They did not sleep for a short part of the night} He said: Al-Hasan said: They did not sleep for a short part of the night."
"6360","(6360) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shakhir, he said: Say Layla She came to them, and they were all healed."
"6361","(6361) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Bastam, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: {The righteous} are the few."
"6362","(6362) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Hasan; {They were hungry for a little while of the night} He said: They were hungry for a little while, then they extended it until dawn."
"6363","(6363) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Al-Hassan, who said: Say, “A night has come upon them.” They made her happy."
"6364","(6364) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: They did not sleep all night."
"6365","(6365) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {They did not feel hungry for a short part of the night.} He said: Say, “There is rarely a night that passes by them unless they pray during it.”"
"6366","(6366) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: {They were} a few people."
"6367","(6367) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; {They did not sleep for a little while of the night} He said: They did not sleep."
"6368","(6368) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih; He said: {They were little. We did not stay overnight until the morning}."
"6369","(6369) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Atiyya, who said: I heard Al-Hasan, and he was asked about the garment coming out of The weaver, does he pray in it? He said: Yes. He said: I heard Ibn Sirin disapproving of it."
"6370","(6370) Waki’ told us, he said: Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm in praying in a Jew’s robe. And the Christian."
"6371","(6371) Waki’ told us, he said: Ali bin Salih told us, on the authority of Ata’ Abi Muhammad, he said: I saw Ali wearing a shirt from This is a nightmare, without washing."
"6372","(6372) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father; That Jabir bin Abdullah prayed in a woven garment."
"6373","(6373) Abu Malik al-Janabi Amr ibn Hashim told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I asked Abu Ja’far about the garment. Does the Jew and Christian wear it, and pray in it? He said: There is no harm in it."
"6374","(6374) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim bin Tarfi, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There will be people who raise their eyes to the heavens in prayer, or not. Return to them. (Muslim 117 Ahmad 5/108)"
"6375","(6375) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: What is the matter with people who raise their eyes to the heavens in their prayer? So he became more intense about that until he said: Let them stop. About that, or their eyes will be snatched away. (Bukhari 750, Abu Dawud 910)"
"6376","(6376) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ammar al-Absi, who said: I heard Ibn Yasar saying: Hudhayfah said: Either One of you fears that when he raises his gaze to the heavens, his sight will not return to him. That is, while he was praying."
"6377","(6377) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, and Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of Tamim bin Salama, who said: Abd said: God: There will surely be people who raise their eyes to the heavens in prayer, or it will not be returned to them."
"6378","(6378) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah; He saw a man raising his gaze to the heavens, and Abdullah said: What does he know about this? Perhaps his sight will shine before he returns to it."
"6379","(6379) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Utbah, on the authority of Shuraih; He saw a man who had raised his hand and his gaze to the heavens, and he said: Retain your hand and lower your gaze, for you will not see him. And you will not get it."
"6380","(6380) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was one of He looks at something while praying, then raises his gaze until a verse is revealed. If it is not this, then I do not know what is: {Those who are humble in their prayer}. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, lowered his head. (Abu Dawud 45. Abdul Razzaq 3262)"
"6381","(6381) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Aisha, she said: What I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, hastening to perform some of the voluntary prayers, such as hastening to perform the two rak’ahs of dawn, Nor any of his spoils. (Bukhari 1169 and Abu Dawud 1248)"
"6382","(6382) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh, who said: I heard Abu Huraira say: No. Skip the two rak'ahs of dawn, even if the horses knock you down."
"6383","(6383) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he said: O Humran, do not skip two rak’ahs before dawn, for in them are the desires."
"6384","(6384) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Omar said about the two rak’ahs before dawn: This is more beloved to me than red camels."
"6385","(6385) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun say: They did not abandon Four rak'ahs before noon, and two rak'ahs before dawn at any time."
"6386","(6386) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: I was informed that Aisha used to say: Take care of The two rak'ahs of Fajr, for in them are goodness and desires."
"6387","(6387) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When two of them, or one of them, prayed and then died, Its parts are the two rak'ahs of Fajr."
"6388","(6388) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, he said: If he prays two rak’ahs Fajr prayer, then he died, as if he had prayed Fajr prayer."
"6389","(6389) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, who said: Al-Hasan considered the two rak’ahs before dawn to be obligatory."
"6390","(6390) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Two rak’ahs of Fajr are better than this world and all that is in it. (Muslim 501, Tirmidhi 416)"
"6391","(6391) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the two rak’ahs at the time of the Iqama, between the call to prayer and the Iqama. (Bukhari 6191, Muslim 501)"
"6392","(6392) Abu Al-Ahwas and Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the two rak’ahs at the time of the call to prayer. One of them said: He performs the Witr prayer when performing the Iqama. (Ibn Majah 1147. Ahmad 1/77)"
"6393","(6393) Ali bin Al-Ja’d told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: It was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the two rak’ahs of Fajr, and it was as if the call to prayer was before his ears. (Bukhari 995. Tirmidhi 461)"
"6394","(6394) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, more than twenty times, reciting in the two rak’ahs before dawn and the two rak’ahs after sunset: {Say, O O you disbelievers}, and {Say: He is God, One}"
"6395","(6395) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in the two rak’ahs of Fajr: {Say, O you disbelievers}, and {Say: Allah is one. He facilitates the recitation between them. (Ahmad 6/184; Abd al-Razzaq 4788)"
"6396","(6396) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, on the authority of Saeed bin Yassar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in the first two rak’ahs of Fajr: “Say, ‘We believe in God and in what has been revealed. To Us} the verse, and in the second: {Come to a word of equal agreement between us and you}"
"6397","(6397) Ibn Aliyah and Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was Ibn Masoud recites in the two rak'ahs before the morning prayer. Or he said: before lunch with: {Say, O disbelievers}, and {Say: He is God, One}. Zaad Ghandar: And in the two rak'ahs after sunset."
"6398","(6398) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Saleel, on the authority of Ghanim ibn Qays, who said: We were commanded to We call out Satan in the two rak'ahs before the morning, or before the morning, with: {Say, O you who are disbelievers}, and {Say: He is Allah. one}"
"6399","(6399) Abbad told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He used to recite in the two rak'ahs before dawn and the two rak'ahs after sunset: with: {Say, O you disbelievers}, And {Say: Allah is One}"
"6400","(6400) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Sirin narrated to me; On the authority of Ibn Sirin; In the two rak'ahs before dawn, he used to recite: {Say, O you disbelievers}, and {Say: He is God, One}."
"6401","(6401) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: They used to recite among them: {Say O you disbelievers}, and {Say: He is God, One}"
"6402","(6402) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah’s companions used to recite in The two rak'ahs before dawn, and the two rak'ahs after sunset: {Say to those who disbelieve}, and {Say: He is Allah, the One}."
"6403","(6403) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Hakim al-Hadrami, on the authority of Talha, On the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla: In the two rak'ahs after sunset, he used to recite: {Say, O disbelievers}, and {Say: He is God, One}."
"6404","(6404) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He used to recite in the two rak'ahs before dawn: {If you are shaken} and {Al-Adiyat}, and in the two rak'ahs after the evening prayer: {Amen. The Messenger"
"6405","(6405) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid; He used to recite in the two rak'ahs before dawn and the two rak'ahs after sunset: {Say, O you disbelievers}, And {Say: Allah is One}"
"6406","(6406) Waki’ narrated to us, Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he shortens the two rak’ahs of Fajr. (Bukhari 626. Muslim 500)"
"6407","(6407) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; When dawn came, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would pray two short rak’ahs."
"6408","(6408) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Aisha said: The standing of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was May the peace and blessings of God be upon him in the two rak’ahs before the morning prayer, according to the fate of the opener of the Book. (Ahmed 217)"
"6409","(6409) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ya’fur, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Sala, who said: I came to Hudhayfy in his house, then We came to the mosque, he prayed two short rak'ahs, then the prayer was established."
"6410","(6410) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They did not pray more than two light rak'ahs when dawn came."
"6411","(6411) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Labid, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, he said: They were The two rak'ahs are shortened before dawn."
"6412","(6412) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Hafsa; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray two light rak’ahs when dawn broke. (Hamidi 288)"
"6413","(6413) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Hafsah told me; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray two light prostrations when dawn broke. (Bukhari 1173. Muslim 89)"
"6414","(6414) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his mother, Amr. On the authority of Aisha, she said: If the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was to pray the two rak’ahs before dawn, then he should shorten them. Even if I were to say: Should I recite from them the Mother of the Book? (Bukhari 1171. Ahmad 6/235)"
"6415","(6415) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Hamid told us, he heard it from Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, he said: I did not see He never led them in prayer, except as if he was hastening to do something."
"6416","(6416) Waki’ told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of a sheikh from the Ansar, Mis’ar said: Uthman showed him, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, may have prolonged the two rak’ahs of dawn."
"6417","(6417) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith Abi Al-Mushrifi, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm in prolonging my rak’ah. Fajr, it is recited from his party if he misses it."
"6418","(6418) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm in prolonging the two rak’ahs of Fajr."
"6419","(6419) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Abraham about the man who used to perform Witr at the end of the night, and he stayed On him from the night? Let him pray for the opening and let him recite. When dawn comes, he performs one rak’ah, then he adds another rak’ah to it, so it is two rak’ahs. Fajr He said: So I mentioned that to Muhammad bin Sirin, and he said: I do not know what this is?"
"6420","(6420) Kathir bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar bin Burqan, who said: I said to Maymun: I recite a long surah at night. So the dawn overtakes me until I have made a very long prayer, then I add another to it, and make it the two rak’ahs of Fajr? He said: Yes."
"6421","(6421) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Jarir ibn Hazim, on the authority of Ali ibn Hakim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If a man wishes, he may open the door. He performed a raka’ah at the end of the night, and he continued it for a long time, until in the morning he raka’ah, then he joined another to it, then he observed the waiting period with both of them. The two rak'ahs of Fajr."
"6422","(6422) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sa’id, on the authority of Salim Abul Nadr, on the authority of Busr bin Sa’id, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best prayer is that a person prays in his home, except for what is prescribed. (Bukhari 6113. Abu Dawud 1442)"
"6423","(6423) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, who said: I saw Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid praying in The mosque, then he leaves before praying anything in it. That means he does not volunteer."
"6424","(6424) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Hudhayfi was asked about voluntary prayers in the mosque? He means after the obligatory prayer, and he said: I hate it, while they are all praying if they disagree."
"6425","(6425) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, saying: I did not see Abraham volunteering in his people’s mosque."
"6426","(6426) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Nasir bin Dha’luq, he said: I did not see Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim volunteering in Al-Hay Qat Mosque."
"6427","(6427) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar, he said: When you pray What is written is in your home."
"6428","(6428) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Nu’man ibn Qays, who said: I have never seen Ubaidah volunteer in a mosque. The living except for bitterness."
"6429","(6429) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, he said: Suwayd bin Ghafali did not He performs a voluntary prayer after another prayer, until he turns around when he is delivered to his house."
"6430","(6430) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man ibn Qays, on the authority of Ubaidah, who said: He did not pray anything in his mosque. After the obligatory prayer."
"6431","(6431) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib and Al-Amri narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the two rak’ahs after sunset in his house. (Bukhari 1180, Tirmidhi 432)"
"6432","(6432) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, he said: It was Abdul Rahman. Ibn Awf prays the two rak'ahs after sunset in his house."
"6433","(6433) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the Mosque of Banu Abd al-Ashhal and led them in the Maghrib prayer. When he greeted him, he said: Bow down. Perform these two rak'ahs in your homes. He said: I saw Mahmoud, who was the imam of his people, leading the Maghrib prayer with them. Then he goes out and sits in the courtyard of the mosque until he gets up before dark, then he enters his house and prays. (Ibn Majah 1165. Ahmad 5/427)"
"6434","(6434) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Al-Abbas bin Sahl al-Sa’idi narrated to us, saying: I have witnessed the time Othman bin Affan, and he was about to say the salaam from Morocco, and I did not see a single man leading them in prayer in the mosque, opening the doors of the mosque until they leave and pray it in their homes."
"6435","(6435) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: They used to recommend performing these two rak’ahs. After sunset in their homes."
"6436","(6436) Umar ibn Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Maimun ibn Mihran, who said: Hudhayfah prayed the Maghrib prayer in In congregation, when the imam said the salaam, a man stood beside him and wanted to pray the two rak’ahs, but Hudhafi pulled him away and said: Sit down. You do not have to delay these two rak’ahs. Wait a little."
"6437","(6437) Umar bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Maimun, who said: They used to like to delay the two rak’ahs after Maghrib until the stars collide."
"6438","(6438) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: When Raja’ bin Hawwah prayed Maghrib, he did not pray after it. anything until the twilight disappears."
"6439","(6439) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the two prostrations before dawn, he would lie down. (Bukhari 6310 and Abu Dawud 1331)"
"6440","(6440) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; That Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, Rafi’ bin Khadij, and Anas bin Malik used to lie down after the two rak’ahs of Fajr."
"6441","(6441) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; That Abu Musa, Rafi’ bin Khadij, and Anas used to do it."
"6442","(6442) Hushaym told us, he said: Ghailan bin Abdullah told us, he said: I saw Ibn Umar praying the two rak’ahs of dawn, then He lay down"
"6443","(6443) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mujahid; That Marwan asked Abu Hurairah about lying down after the two rak’ahs of dawn? He said: No, until you lie down."
"6444","(6444) Hassan bin Abdul Rahman Al Harithi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; When he prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr, he would lie down."
"6445","(6445) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim; Urwa entered the mosque while the people were praying, so he bowed two rak’ahs, then his side touched the ground, then he got up and entered with the people. Prayer"
"6446","(6446) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I accompanied Ibn Umar while traveling and attending, and what I saw him lying down after the two rak'ahs of dawn."
"6447","(6447) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: Abraham hated lying down after He prays the two rak'ahs before dawn."
"6448","(6448) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Omar saw A man lay down after two rak'ahs and said: Count him, or did you not count him?"
"6449","(6449) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: What is the matter with the man when Pray the two rak'ahs and enjoy yourself as animals and donkeys enjoy you? If he greets, he has prayed."
"6450","(6450) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Majlaz, he said: I asked Ibn Omar about the man lying On his right hand after the two rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer? He said: Satan is playing with you."
"6451","(6451) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr said: Do not lie down after the two rak’ahs before dawn, but lie down after the Witr prayer."
"6452","(6452) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Issa al-Kabbat narrated to us, saying: I heard Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab saying: What is the matter with one of you when He prayed the two rak'ahs while wallowing? The greeting is sufficient."
"6453","(6453) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He laid down. Satan"
"6454","(6454) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; It was not surprising for him to lie down after the two rak'ahs of dawn."
"6455","(6455) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, he said: Ibn Umar saw Some people lay down after the two dawn rak'ahs, so he sent for them and comforted them, and they said: We want to follow that Sunnah. Then Ibn Umar said: Go back to them and tell them that it is an innovation."
"6456","(6456) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Yazid; When he prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr, he used to hide himself."
"6457","(6457) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn and Mughiry told us, on the authority of Ibrahim. Abdullah said: What is this wallowing? After the two rak'ahs of dawn, it is like the wallowing of a donkey."
"6458","(6458) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Nadr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Peace and blessings of God be upon him, when he prays the two rak’ahs of Fajr, if you are awake, speak to me, otherwise lie down. (Bukhari 1161, Muslim 511)"
"6459","(6459) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Umari told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Perhaps Ibn Omar spoke after the two rak’ahs of Fajr."
"6460","(6460) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in him becoming a Muslim. He speaks the Hajj after the two rak’ahs of Fajr."
"6461","(6461) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They did not see any harm in speaking after the two rak'ahs of Fajr."
"6462","(6462) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ibn Masoud saw a man talking to another after... You performed the dawn rak'ahs, and he said: Either you remember Allah or you remain silent."
"6463","(6463) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: No one I forced him to speak after the two rak’ahs of Fajr until he prayed the morning prayer from Ibn Masoud."
"6464","(6464) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Al-Masoudi narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: It was Abdullah It is difficult for him to hear someone speaking after dawn, meaning after the two rak'ahs, except with the Qur’an, or with the remembrance of God, until He prays."
"6465","(6465) Muammar bin Sulaiman Al-Ruqi told us, on the authority of Khaseef, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He used to hate speaking after the two rak'ahs of Fajr, unless God was mentioned."
"6466","(6466) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Khusayf, he said: I asked Sa`id bin Jubayr about a verse after The two rak'ahs of Fajr? He did not answer me, so when he prayed, he said: Speech is disliked after them."
"6467","(6467) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Do not speak after the two rak’ahs of Fajr. And dawn, unless you have a need."
"6468","(6468) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to hate speaking after The two rak'ahs of Fajr. He said: I said to Abraham: What did the man say to his family: “Prayer”? He said: No problem."
"6469","(6469) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’ (h) and on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; They disliked speaking after the two rak'ahs of dawn."
"6470","(6470) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Quraysh, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: I saw Ibn Umar praying two rak’ahs. Fajr, then he hid himself and did not speak until he prayed the morning prayer."
"6471","(6471) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, who said: Jabir bin Zayd was asked: Is there a difference between The Fajr prayer and between the two rak’ahs do you say anything before them? He said: No, unless he speaks about a need if he wants."
"6472","(6472) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Husayn and Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq; He entered the mosque while the people were in the morning prayer, and he had not prayed the two rak'ahs, so they prayed in a corner, then he entered With the people in their prayers."
"6473","(6473) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He used to say: They would pray in one place, then he would enter with The people in their prayers."
"6474","(6474) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He came to the mosque with the imam in the dawn prayer, so he prayed the two rak’ahs before entering the mosque, at the door of The mosque"
"6475","(6475) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, he said: Abu Uthman told me, he said: I saw the man coming and Omar Ibn Al-Khattab is in the Fajr prayer, so he prays the two rak’ahs next to the mosque, then he joins the people in their prayer."
"6476","(6476) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Mudarib; Ibn Masoud and Abu Musa left Sa`id bin Al-Aas, and the prayer was performed, so Ibn Masoud bowed two rak'ahs, then He entered the prayer with the people, and as for Abu Musa, he entered the row."
"6477","(6477) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Ibrahim, who said: I said to Tawus: Should I perform the two rak’ahs and the one performing the prayer should perform the prayer? He said: Can you do that?"
"6478","(6478) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Ikrim, who said: Read, and do not read, and if you read, then reduce it. Pray them even on the road, meaning the two rak’ahs of Fajr."
"6479","(6479) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you enter the mosque and the people are in it, Fajr prayer, and you have not performed the two rak’ahs of Fajr, then perform them, and if you think that you will miss the first rak’ah, you will miss them."
"6480","(6480) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Dulham bin Salih, on the authority of Bura, who said: I saw Ibn Umar doing it, and someone narrated to me He saw it and did it twice; He came once while they were praying, so they prayed next to the mosque, then he entered another time and prayed with them, but he did not pray with them."
"6481","(6481) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; If he came and the imam was performing the Fajr prayer, he disliked that they should lead them in prayer in the mosque, and he said: They should lead them in prayer at the door of The mosque, or around it."
"6482","(6482) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Abi Malik, on the authority of Abu Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abu Darda’, He said: I will come to the people while they are in rows for the dawn prayer, and I will pray the two rak’ahs, then I will join them."
"6483","(6483) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he used to say about the man If he enters the mosque and the people are praying the morning prayer, he says: He enters with the people in their prayer, and he does not pray the two rak’ahs. What he misses from the obligatory prayer is greater than the two rak’ahs."
"6484","(6484) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I mentioned it to Abraham, and he said: What is written will be fulfilled, and he passed on Volunteering"
"6485","(6485) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Salamah ibn Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: What is missed from the imam’s prayer is better. Of what is required in your prayer is the two rak’ahs."
"6486","(6486) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Asim Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Hammad, who said: Do not enter the mosque until you have prayed two rak’ahs before Fajr, even if it is at dawn."
"6487","(6487) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Hasan, who said: I saw Ibn Maqil praying the two rak’ahs before Fajr in the rain."
"6488","(6488) Mulazim bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Bashir bin Farroukh, he said: Ayyub bin Utba narrated to me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abu Kathir said: Whoever comes to the mosque and the prayer has been established, let him delay the two rak’ahs before dawn until dawn. He prays for them as a sacrifice."
"6489","(6489) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, he said: If he was in a place They both prayed, and if he was in the mosque, he did not pray for them."
"6490","(6490) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he was afraid to miss a rak’ah, he would enter with them. And he did not pray for them."
"6491","(6491) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque and took Bilal in it. Iqama, so Ibn Buhaynah stood up and prayed two rak’ahs, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, struck his shoulder and said: O Ibn Al-Qashb, you pray four four hours in the morning. (Bayhaqi 482)"
"6492","(6492) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Hafs, on the authority of Ibn Buhayna, he said The morning prayer was performed, and a man stood up to pray the two rak’ahs. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed, the people around him lamented. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the one who prayed the two rak’ahs: Do you pray four rak’ahs in the morning? (Bukhari 663 and Muslim 493)"
"6493","(6493) Yazid bin Harun told us, saying: Abu Aamir Al-Muzani Salih bin Rustum told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The morning prayer was performed, so he stood up?? A man was praying the two rak'ahs, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pulled his garment and said: Do you pray four rak'ahs in the morning? (Ahmad 1/355, Abu Ali 2568)"
"6494","(6494) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, who said: Ibrahim said: Because I may realize what has escaped me from The written books are more beloved to me than that I pray them both."
"6495","(6495) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated to provide support to the tribe. After the two rak'ahs of Fajr."
"6496","(6496) Hushaym told us, saying: Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman; Ibn Masoud entered the mosque and saw people who had joined forces towards the qiblah. He said: Then Abdullah said to them: Like this, in front of the faces of the angels?"
"6497","(6497) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: When dawn came, Ibn Umar used to pray Two rak'ahs, then he would hide while we were around him. If he saw one of us slumbering, he would move him. He said: He was slumbering while he was hiding. Then the prayer is performed, and he gets up and prays."
"6498","(6498) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, who said: Abdullah entered the mosque for the dawn prayer. Then, behold, a people had leaned their backs toward the qiblah, and he said: Move aside from the qiblah. Do not come between the angels and Her prayer, and these two rak’ahs are the prayer of the angels."
"6499","(6499) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: Whoever walks to the mosque in the darkness of the night will meet God in the light of the Day of Resurrection. (Darimi 1422, Ibn Hibban 2046)"
"6500","(6500) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to see Walking in the dark night is obligatory."
"6501","(6501) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Saeed, he said: Muhammad bin Ibrahim narrated to me, on the authority of Qays bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw a man praying two rak’ahs after the morning prayer, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: The morning prayer twice? Then the man said: I had not prayed the two rak’ahs before them, so I prayed them now, so I remained silent. (Tirmidhi 422 and Abu Dawud 1261)"
"6502","(6502) Hushaym told us, saying: Abdul-Malik told us about Ata’; That a man prayed the morning prayer with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the prayer, he stood up. The man prayed two rak'ahs, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What are these two rak'ahs? He said: O Messenger of God, I came while you were praying, and I had not prayed the two rak’ahs before dawn, so I thought that I prayed them while you were praying, and when I finished the prayer, I got up and prayed the prayer, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed at you. He did not command it, nor did he prohibit it. (Tabarani 939)"
"6503","(6503) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: A sheikh, called: Musma’ ibn Thabit, narrated to us, saying: I saw ‘Ata’ do something like: That"
"6504","(6504) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If she missed the two rak’ahs of Fajr, he prayed after the prayer. Fajr"
"6505","(6505) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: I heard Al-Qasim saying: If I had not prayed them Until I prayed Fajr, I prayed them after sunrise."
"6506","(6506) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Ghazwan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He came to the people while they were praying, and he had not prayed the two rak’ahs, so he entered with them, then he sat in his prayer, so when Adha rose and fulfilled them."
"6507","(6507) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, and Rabi’, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He prayed after the sacrifice."
"6508","(6508) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: The two rak’ahs of dawn should not be made up."
"6509","(6509) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Marzuq, on the authority of Atiya, who said: I saw Ibn Umar judging them when the imam greeted them."
"6510","(6510) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Zayd ibn Khalid al-Janni, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Pray in your homes, and do not make them graves. (Abdullah bin Hamid 275 Bazzar 706)"
"6511","(6511) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: If one of you performs the prayer in your mosque, let him make his house a share of his prayers, for God is the one who will put in it. His verse of prayer is better. (Muslim 539. Ahmad 3/316)"
"6512","(6512) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidi, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Sa’id; On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, like the hadith of Abu Muawiyah. (Ahmad 3/59; Abd al-Razzaq 4837)"
"6513","(6513) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him, he said: Pray in your homes, and do not make them graves. (Bukhari 1187, Muslim 538)"
"6514","(6514) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sa’id, on the authority of Salim Abul Nadr, on the authority of Busr bin Sa’id, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The best prayer is the prayer of a person in his home, except for what is written."
"6515","(6515) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Abdullah’s best prayer was in his house."
"6516","(6516) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Damra bin Habib, on the authority of a man From the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: A man’s voluntary prayers in his home are greater than his voluntary prayers among the people, as a virtue. A man’s prayer in congregation is superior to his prayer alone."
"6517","(6517) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: There was Shurayh and Masruq, both of them had a house. It prolongs the prayer."
"6518","(6518) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, who said: A man’s prayer in the presence of his family. The secret"
"6519","(6519) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not turn your homes into graves. (Muslim 539. Tirmidhi 2877)"
"6520","(6520) Shababā told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Salih, the client of the twins, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib ibn Khabab, he said: I used to only pray in the mosque, and Zaid bin Thabit said to me: A man’s prayer in his home is better than his prayer in the mosque. Except for what is written, and a man’s prayer in his house is light."
"6521","(6521) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Asim bin Amr; That a group of people from Iraq came to Omar and asked him about the man’s prayer in his house? Omar said: No one has asked me about it since I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about it. He said: The man’s prayer in His house is light, so enlighten your homes."
"6522","(6522) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, he said: The companions of Abdullah They say: The front row next to Al-Maqsourah."
"6523","(6523) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, who said: I heard Abu Ubaidah say: The first row The one next to Al-Maqsourah."
"6524","(6524) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I saw Abu Abd al-Rahman, Zirr ibn Hubaysh, and Amr ibn Maymun. They pray to the right of the maqsourah, and Hafs once said: What is between the two cylinders and the wall?"
"6525","(6525) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad narrated to us, saying: I said to Al-Hasan: They say: The first row. He is the one next to the shrine. He said: He is the one next to the wall."
"6526","(6526) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salma bin Wardan, who said: I saw a man praying at the stone."
"6527","(6527) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and he narrated it: He said: Do not follow a sleeping person, nor Speaking"
"6528","(6528) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Mujahid; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade praying behind those who sleep and talk. (Tabarani 5242)"
"6529","(6529) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith narrated to us, he said: I was sitting Next to Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, he turned and saw a man praying behind him, and he said to him: Either he has turned away, or To stand up for you"
"6530","(6530) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hudha’i, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Saeed bin Wahhab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud ; He hated to follow people who talked."
"6531","(6531) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Maadi Karb, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Do not follow. With a people who dispute, or confuse."
"6532","(6532) Umar ibn Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: Ibn Umar would not pray behind a man who was not praying, except On Friday. He said: So I mentioned that to Abd al-Karim, and he said: Ibn Umar would not pray behind a man who was speaking except on the day of Friday prayer."
"6533","(6533) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Ash-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: If They used to talk about the remembrance of God, so there is no harm in him following them."
"6534","(6534) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It is more beloved to me to pray behind someone sitting than I pray while someone is sleeping."
"6535","(6535) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’ bin Subaih narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Tawus; He hated to follow the prayer while asleep."
"6536","(6536) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik; Omar ibn al-Khattab saw a man praying wearing a hood, the lining of which was made of fox skins. He said: So he threw it off his head. And he said: What makes you know that maybe he is not intelligent?"
"6537","(6537) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali; He hated to pray in fox skins."
"6538","(6538) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr (h) and on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Al-Hasan, they both said: Wear fox skins, and do not pray in them."
"6539","(6539) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw nothing wrong with it if it was tanned."
"6540","(6540) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, he said: I saw Abu Al-Aaliyah entering the mosque. So he prayed in it, and he was wearing a hood lined with fox skins, so he took it from his head and put it in his sleeve, and when He finished his prayer. He said: I said to him: I saw you take your hood off your head and put it on your sleeve? He said: I hated to pray in it, and I hated to leave it and have it stolen, so I put it in the sleeve of my shirt."
"6541","(6541) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sudair al-Sayrifi, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: It was Ali bin al-Hussein’s. A fox's snake wears it, but when he prays he takes it off."
"6542","(6542) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’i, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Saeed bin Wahhab, on the authority of His father; That Ali saw a people praying while they were praying, and he said: It is as if the Jews came out of their culture."
"6543","(6543) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He disliked a man lowering his garment during prayer."
"6544","(6544) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He disliked the saddle."
"6545","(6545) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Fudail bin Ghazwan narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He hated to slow down during prayer, in opposition to the Jews, and he said: They slow down."
"6546","(6546) Ibn Aliyah and Hushaym told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; He hated to pray while praying."
"6547","(6547) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; They both disliked slowing down during prayer. Waki` said: And we hate it."
"6548","(6548) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asal bin Sufyan, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Huraira; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade leaning during prayer. (Tirmidhi 378, Ahmad 2/295)"
"6549","(6549) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; He did not see any harm in barring."
"6550","(6550) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Most of the time I have seen a donor give back."
"6551","(6551) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; He saw no harm in it if he was wearing a shirt."
"6552","(6552) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Muharib, who said: I saw Ibn Umar descending in Prayer"
"6553","(6553) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Shihab Musa bin Thabit narrated to us, saying: I saw Sa`id bin Jubayr descending in Voluntary, and it is a sufficient source of income."
"6554","(6554) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad; He used to recite the prayer in prayer."
"6555","(6555) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: I saw Al-Hassan reciting the prayer more than I can count, and I saw It appears"
"6556","(6556) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zaid bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm in praying."
"6557","(6557) Muadh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, he said: I saw Muhammad praying and he had lowered his garment, but I do not know what the garment was on. It was, or on the shirt."
"6558","(6558) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, who said: I saw Ibn Sirin reciting the prayer."
"6559","(6559) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: I saw an alcoholic man putting his tongue on him during prayer."
"6560","(6560) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam; He saw no harm."
"6561","(6561) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mahdi bin Maimun, who said: I saw Al-Hasan descending upon Al-Quba’i."
"6562","(6562) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: I asked Muslim bin Yasar: Where is his end? Sight during prayer? He said: Wherever you prostrate, it is good."
"6563","(6563) Hushaym told us, he said: The common people told us, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Nakha’i; He liked for the person praying not to let his gaze go beyond the place of his prostration."
"6564","(6564) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hurra, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He liked for the man to put his gaze on the shoe of the place of his prostration, and if he did not do that, or to speak something similar. Let him close his eyes."
"6565","(6565) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; He disliked a man praying with his eyes closed."
"6566","(6566) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Jamil bin Ubaid told us, he said: I heard Al-Hasan, and a man asked him: Close my eyes. When I prostrate? He said: If you wish."
"6567","(6567) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Jamil, who said: I heard Al-Hasan, and he was asked about a man who closed his eyes while... Prostrating in prayer? He said: There is no harm in it."
"6568","(6568) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Burd bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Fakhita, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Shadd. Your rights during prayer, even with a shackle."
"6569","(6569) Abdă told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He would not pray unless he was wearing his robe."
"6570","(6570) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I saw Salem bin Abdullah praying with his apron over his shirt. Or he said: I brought it."
"6571","(6571) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Abu Malik; He used to bind his loins during prayer with a thread or something."
"6572","(6572) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, who said: I said to Ibrahim: Should I pray at night wearing a shirt and robes? He said: Girdle your loins with the garment."
"6573","(6573) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Girdle your loins, even if it is with a band."
"6574","(6574) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Ata al-Bakai, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Asam, who said: It was said: Girdle your loins, even with a band."
"6575","(6575) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Waddah; They traveled with Jabir bin Zayd, and he used to lead them with his niqab over his shirt."
"6576","(6576) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; It was disliked for men and women to pray without clothing."
"6577","(6577) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Jair bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; I asked him about a man who prays wearing a robe over his shirt? He said: There is no harm in it."
"6578","(6578) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, who said: Girdle your loins, even if With a headband"
"6579","(6579) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Girdle your loins with something."
"6580","(6580) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Thaqif, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Girdle your loins, even with a shackle."
"6581","(6581) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Ibn Al-Aswad, and Ibrahim; Indeed, they believed without a cloak."
"6582","(6582) Hushaym told us, saying: Mujalid told us; Abu Habira Al-Ansari asked Al-Sha’bi, and he said: Should I tighten my loins when I stand up to pray? Al-Sha’bi said to him: Only the Magi do that."
"6583","(6583) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik, who said: If you tie the robes over you, I will reward you with the part of the garment."
"6584","(6584) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Hassan, who said: I saw Abu Al-Bakhtari praying in a qaba’."
"6585","(6585) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Suwayd, he said: He presented Black is from a journey, so he prayed wearing a qabaya."
"6586","(6586) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, who said: Hudhayfy prayed in a shop while they were Lower than him, he said: So Salman pulled him until he let him down, and when he left, he said to him: Did you not know that your companions were haters? For the imam to pray over something, while they are lower than it? He said: Hudhayfy said: Yes, I mentioned it when you supported me."
"6587","(6587) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Hudhayfah prayed over a shop in Al-Mada’in, higher than His companions, so Abu Masoud reached out to him and said to him: Did you not know that this was disliked? He said: Didn't you see that when you mentioned me, I mentioned you?"
"6588","(6588) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Huzayl, on the authority of Abdullah; He hated for the Imam to rise above his companions."
"6589","(6589) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Shadhrawan of the palace used to stand for the imam. He said: Abdullah hated it, and ordered it to be broken."
"6590","(6590) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated that the position of the Imam was higher than that of the people, and he hated that a man should be elevated in status. He prayed something to prostrate upon."
"6591","(6591) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Bilal Al-Absi, who said: Ammar saw a man He was praying upon his master, so he took the back of it and lowered it to the ground and said: Pray here."
"6592","(6592) Waki’ told us, he said: Othman bin Abi Hind told us, he said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz praying above A church in the Levant, while the people are lower than it."
"6593","(6593) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He saw no harm in the imam praying in a place higher than His companions"
"6594","(6594) Abu Bakr bin Ayash and Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The imam of the people is a guarantor. He should not single out any of his supplications on their behalf."
"6595","(6595) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, he said: Abu Qalaab said: Do you know why you disliked the imamate? He said: No, but we disliked it because an imam does not have the right to single out a supplication for himself rather than those behind him."
"6596","(6596) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is disliked for the imam to assign anything to himself rather than His companions"
"6597","(6597) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Harun bin Ibrahim, who said: I said to Ibn Sirin: The imam should specify With some supplication? He said: No, so let him pray for them as he prays for himself."
"6598","(6598) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos and Mujahid, who said: The imam should not He specializes in supplications for himself on behalf of the people."
"6599","(6599) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Kurdous, on the authority of Abdullah; Indeed, if a man was among the people, he disliked him singling out any of the supplications for himself rather than them."
"6600","(6600) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: I don’t care whether I blow, or I speak."
"6601","(6601) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; He hated blowing it during prayer, and he said: blow it with your garment, or with the sleeve of your shirt. And he hated blowing it."
"6602","(6602) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ibn Abi Al-Hudhayl, he said: Because I prostrate on the kneecaps, I am more beloved to me. To blow in my prayer."
"6603","(6603) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hudhayl, he said: Because I put my forehead On a coal until it is extinguished is more beloved to me than blowing during my prayer and then prostrating."
"6604","(6604) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: The blowing in prayer is speech."
"6605","(6605) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The blowing in The prayer interrupts the prayer."
"6606","(6606) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; He disliked blowing it during prayer."
"6607","(6607) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He hated blowing it during prayer."
"6608","(6608) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Husayn; Abu Abd al-Rahman disliked blowing it during prayer."
"6609","(6609) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, who said: It was said: It is indecency for a man to blow his mouth. His prayers"
"6610","(6610) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan Al-Asfari, who said: I prayed in the Ash-Sha’abi chamber, and I blew, and he cursed me. And he said: If you see any harm, wipe it with your hand."
"6611","(6611) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Abu Saleh; A relative of Umm Salamah prayed and blew, and Umm Salama said: Do not do it, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a boy of ours: Black, it is said to him: Rabah: Rabah of your face. (Tirmidhi 382. Ahmad 6/323)"
"6612","(6612) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir; He disliked blowing it during prayer."
"6613","(6613) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Laith: He saw Mujahid faltering in prayer."
"6614","(6614) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abul-Safar, who said: We met the old men of the neighborhood and the youth. They encourage them in prayer."
"6615","(6615) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ubaidah bin Nabul, his servant Aisha bin Saad, she said: I saw Aisha bin Saad removes her armor during prayer. What do you go with?"
"6616","(6616) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Harun ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: There is no harm in going for a walk. Prayer"
"6617","(6617) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated it in vain, and did not see any harm in it during the severity of the heat."
"6618","(6618) Abdullah bin Mubarak and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim bin Yasar, on the authority of his father; He disliked moving forward during prayer."
"6619","(6619) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Abd al-Karim Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Umair, who said: I wandered. Between Abi Al-Aliyah and Muslim bin Yasar, he denied me."
"6620","(6620) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibrahim; He disliked moving forward during prayer."
"6621","(6621) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, and Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Salami; He disliked moving forward during prayer."
"6622","(6622) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: We used to fight with his soldiers bin Abi. The sea was swollen, so we used to pray sitting on the ship."
"6623","(6623) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, that Ibn Sirin said: I went out with Anas to Banu Sirin in two ships. Great He said: So we believed, so he prayed two rak'ahs with us sitting there, then he led another two rak'ahs with us."
"6624","(6624) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab; He saw no harm in praying while sitting on the ship."
"6625","(6625) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Khuzaymah, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Pray in it while sitting."
"6626","(6626) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: Anas was asked about praying on a ship? Abdullah bin Abi Utba, Anas’s client, who was sitting with us, said: I traveled with Abu Sa’id al-Khudri and Abu al-Darda’. And Jabir bin Abdullah, Humayd said: And some people he named, so our imam used to lead us in prayer standing on the ship, and we pray. He stood behind him, and if we had wished, we would have departed."
"6627","(6627) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim bin Yassar, on the authority of his father; That his father used to set up a flag on the ship and pray standing, and it was raised with its sails running."
"6628","(6628) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, they said: Pray in the ship, standing upright. Al-Hasan said: Do not be difficult for your companions."
"6629","(6629) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he said regarding prayer in the ship: If you wish, stand. If you wish, you can sit, but standing is better."
"6630","(6630) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, that he said: He should pray while standing on the ship, and if he is not able to do so, then sitting, and prostrate on a place on it."
"6631","(6631) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Pray in it, standing."
"6632","(6632) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Pray in the ship, standing upright."
"6633","(6633) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I asked Abraham about prayer in a ship? He said: If he is able to go out, let him go out, otherwise let him pray standing, and if he is able, otherwise let him pray sitting and facing. The kiss whenever it is distorted."
"6634","(6634) Ibn Abi Ghaniya told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: He should pray in it standing, if he is not able So he is sitting, and if he is able to go out in the grave, let him go out."
"6635","(6635) Waki’ told us, he said: Hassan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, who said: He sets up a flag on the ship and then He follows him."
"6636","(6636) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Ala’ ibn Qais Al-Kaili told us, he said: I asked Ata’ about praying on a ship? He said: Do not pray in it as long as you find it difficult."
"6637","(6637) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He faces the qiblah whenever it is distorted."
"6638","(6638) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They circle with the qiblah wherever The ship turned around."
"6639","(6639) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: He made tayammum facing the direction wherever the ship turned."
"6640","(6640) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabi’ bin Subaih narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, who said: They pray standing therein. collectively, and they revolve with the tribe wherever it turns."
"6641","(6641) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala’, who said: I heard Ata’, and he was asked about a mariner who was on a ship. And his family is with him there, and this is his residence, and he travels there? He said: He prays four times in it."
"6642","(6642) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Al-Hasan was asked about the sailors being on the ship with their families. Do you complete the prayer? He said: Yes, these are their homes."
"6643","(6643) Waki’ told us, he said: Iyas bin Daghfal told us, he said: I asked Ata’ about praying on a ship? He said: They are assured."
"6644","(6644) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hawshab bin Aqeel Al-Abdi, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about the Magian navigator who was among The hands of the people are in the ship while they are praying, and He is standing? He said: He prays behind him, even if he is standing."
"6645","(6645) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Ata; About the Magi navigators who are among the people on the ship while they are praying? He said: There is no harm in it."
"6646","(6646) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of a man called: Yazid, on the authority of Ammar bin Yasir. ; He fainted during the noon, afternoon, sunset, and evening prayers, so he woke up some part of the night and made them up."
"6647","(6647) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: It was said to Imran bin Husayn: Indeed, Samurah bin Jundub He says regarding a fainting woman: He will make up for every prayer like it, so Imran said: It is not as he said, he will make up for all of them."
"6648","(6648) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, and Ash’ath, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He had been unconscious for several days, so he repeated the prayers of the day during which he regained consciousness, and did not repeat anything from what he had done."
"6649","(6649) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He fainted. Wakee’ said: I see him saying: It was a month, so he prayed his day’s prayer."
"6650","(6650) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid, that they said about fainting. Ali: He performs his prayers as he performs Ramadan."
"6651","(6651) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He will perform the prayers on that day. He woke up in it."
"6652","(6652) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: I asked him about the one who passed out. He woke up? He said: He completes the prayers of the day during which he woke up."
"6653","(6653) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: When a man faints He did not repeat two prayers, and if he fainted, he repeated one prayer."
"6654","(6654) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He used to say about the one who passed out: If he fainted for a day or night, he should repeat it, and if it was more than that, he would not repeat it."
"6655","(6655) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: If a man fainted for several days then regained consciousness, He completed his day and night’s prayers."
"6656","(6456) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Majashar; Maymun was of the opinion that the unconscious man should perform the prayer as he performs the fast."
"6657","(6657) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: He fainted for several days. He did not return anything."
"6658","(6658) Hushaym told us, he said: Juwaybir told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: He fainted while praying, so it was said to him: It is Since such-and-such a prayer, he has performed such-and-such prayers. He said: Then he said: Nothing has departed from me, nor has it returned."
"6659","(6659) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A person who has passed out may make up the fast, but he does not make it up. Prayer, just as a menstruating woman is required to make up for the fast but not for the prayer."
"6660","(6660) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: A person who has passed out should not be made up. With the mothers of the believers, they did not make up for it during their menstruation."
"6661","(6661) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: A person who has passed out is not judged. He said: Ibn Sirin fainted for several days and did not make up for it."
"6662","(6662) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Omari narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He fainted for two days and did not make up for it."
"6663","(6663) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning the one who passed out, he said: He does not have to bring him back."
"6664","(6664) Waki` narrated to us, and that which people take to heart is the one who faints for days and does not make up for anything except one prayer. The day on which he woke up is like a menstruating woman, and the one who fainted for one day should perform the prayers of that day."
"6665","(6665) Waki’ told us, he said: Yazid bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed that it was stolen. He carries milk with him on the ship, meaning he prostrates on it."
"6666","(6666) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad; When Masruq traveled, he would carry milk with him on the ship and prostrate on it."
"6667","(6667) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; He hated to prostrate on the two planks attached to the ship."
"6668","(6668) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Amer Al-Muzani told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Pray four times during the night, pray even if it is two rak’ahs. There is not a household who is known to have prayed during the night without him calling them. Caller: O People of the House: Arise for your prayers."
"6669","(6669) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He had mercy. May God have mercy on a man who got up during the night and prayed, then he woke up his family and they prayed. May God have mercy on a woman who got up during the night and prayed, then She woke up her husband and they prayed. (Abu Dawud 1445. Ahmad 2/250)"
"6670","(6670) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Al-Ashhab told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Pray during the night even if Aleppo is as hot as tea."
"6671","(6671) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad; It was desirable for a man not to neglect the night prayer, even if he had the power to milk a sheep."
"6672","(6672) Abd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Murr, he said: Abdullah said: The superiority of the night prayer over Daytime prayer, like the superiority of secret charity over public charity."
"6673","(6673) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Abdullah bin Rahimah, on the authority of his grandmother, who said: Othman used to fast. Eternity, and the night lasts except in agony from the beginning."
"6674","(6674) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: It was mentioned when The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a man. It was said: O Messenger of God, so-and-so slept all night until morning. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: That is a man in whose ear or ears Satan urinated. (Bukhari 1144, Muslim 537)"
"6675","(6675) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, on the authority of al-Aghar Abi Muslim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, And Abu Sa`id, they said: If a man wakes his wife up in the night and they pray, they are recorded as remembering God often. And memories."
"6676","(6676) Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: Which night is best? He said: The middle of the night."
"6677","(6677) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; That a man asked Abu Dharr: What night do I hear? He said: The middle of the night. He said: Who can tolerate that? He said: Whoever is afraid will fall in."
"6678","(6678) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Burda, on the authority of his father; That Muadh said to Abu Musa: How do you read the Qur’an? He said: I surpass you in great ways. Then Abu Musa said to him: How do you recite it, O Muadh? He said: I sleep at the beginning of the night, and I will strengthen myself for the end of it, and I hope for the reward in my sleep as I hope for it when I am awake. (Bukhari 4341. Muslim 15)"
"6679","(6679) Abd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Aoun bin Abd Allah, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abd Allah bin Utbah, who said: When the eyes were calm, Abdullah would stand up, and I would hear him making a noise like the sound of bees, until the morning."
"6680","(6680) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Salma bin Yahya bin Talha, on the authority of his paternal aunt, Umm Ishaq bint Talha, she said: Al-Hasan bin Ali used to take his share of the night prayers from the beginning of the night, and he Al-Hussein takes his share at the end of the night."
"6681","(6681) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Whenever Ibn Umar woke up, The night was prayed."
"6682","(6682) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Hurr told us, he said: Al-Hasan told us, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, She said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would get up at night to pray, he would begin his prayer with two light rak’ahs. (Muslim 1971, Ahmad 6/30)"
"6683","(6683) Hushaym told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Abu Hurairah said: When he rises If one of you begins the night, let him begin with two light rak'ahs."
"6684","(6684) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I have not seen him start a prayer voluntarily except with two rak’ahs. Two light"
"6685","(6685) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to open his night prayers with two light rak’ahs. (Muslim 1988, Abu Dawud 1317)"
"6686","(6686) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: The night prayer is two by two. (Bukhari 1137, Muslim 146)"
"6687","(6687) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: The night prayer is two by two. (Bukhari 990, Abu Dawud 1320)"
"6688","(6688) Hushaym told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The night prayer is two by two. (Muslim 148. Ahmad 2/58)"
"6689","(6689) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the client of the family of Talha, on the authority of Abu Salama, who said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says the salutation in every two rak’ahs of the night prayer."
"6690","(6690) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Amr, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, he said: In every Two rak'ahs of prayer."
"6691","(6691) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Walid al-Shinni, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Between every two rak’ahs there is a salutation."
"6692","(6692) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, on the authority of Salem, that he said: The night prayer is two by two."
"6693","(6693) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The night prayer is two by two."
"6694","(6694) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The night prayer is two by two."
"6695","(6695) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Raja’, on the authority of Qubaisyah bin Dhu’ayb, who said: He passed by me. Abu Hurairah while I was praying, and he said: Separate, but I did not know what he said, so when I left, I said: What should I separate? He said: Separate the night prayer from the day prayer."
"6696","(6696) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I asked Abraham about the night prayer? He said: It is sufficient for you to recite the Tashahhud in every two rak’ahs, unless you have a need."
"6697","(6697) Waki’ and Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Ali al-Azdi, on the authority of Ibn Umar, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: The night and day prayers are two rak’ahs, two rak’ahs. However, Ghandar said: Two by two. (Nasa’i 472. Ahmad 26)"
"6698","(6698) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to pray four times during the day."
"6699","(6699) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya, that he said: Four by four."
"6700","(6700) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abraham, who said: The daytime prayer is four quarters. This is voluntary."
"6701","(6701) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Nafi’ about performing voluntary prayers during the daytime fire? He said: As for me, I will pray four times. So I mentioned it to Muhammad, and he said: Doesn’t he pray two rak’ahs? Save"
"6702","(6702) Ibrahim bin Sadiqa told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The night and day prayers are two by two."
"6703","(6703) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hanzala bin Abdul Karim, who said: I asked Hammad about the daytime prayer? He said: Two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs."
"6704","(6704) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Amr, who said: Sa`id ibn Jubayr was He prays night and day two by two."
"6705","(6705) Hushaym told us, he said: Ali bin Ata told us, he said: Jabir bin Zayd bin Al-Aswad told me. Al-Amiri, on the authority of his father, said: I witnessed his proof with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I prayed with him in the morning. Al-Khaif Mosque,\n When he finished his prayer and turned away, he found two men at the back of the people who did not pray with him. He said: So he said: I have to take them. So he brought them while their prayers were shaking, and he said: What prevented you from praying with us? They said: O Messenger of God, we had prayed in our travels. He said: Do not do that, if you prayed in your travels and then came. A congregational mosque and pray with them, for they are both voluntary prayers for you."
"6706","(6706) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Uthman, and Abi Al-Umays, on the authority of Uthman bin Ubaidullah bin Abi Rafi’, On the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: His first prayer."
"6707","(6707) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: His first prayer is the obligatory prayer. And this is voluntary."
"6708","(6708) Hushaym told us, he said: Ismail bin Salem told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I heard him say that as well."
"6709","(6709) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Al-Araj, he said: I came to Ibn Omar, and the people were in The noon prayer, so I thought he was not in a state of ritual purity, so I said to him: O Abu Abdul Rahman, shall I bring you a ritual purity? He said: I have undergone ablution and I have prayed, so which one should I seek reward for? Yunus said: So I mentioned that to Al-Hasan, and he said: May God have mercy on Abu Abdul-Rahman, so he made the first one written and this one. Supererogatory"
"6710","(6710) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When a man prays Alone, then he prayed in congregation, so the obligatory prayer is the first."
"6711","(6711) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: If I prayed in my house, then... I came to a congregational mosque, then I performed one rak’ah with it, which was more beloved to me than the prayers I had prayed alone."
"6712","(6712) Hushaym told us, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: The prayer he prayed in congregation."
"6713","(6713) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabah ibn Abi Marouf, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he prayed in congregation, and he had previously prayed Alone, his last prayer."
"6714","(6714) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The obligatory prayer means congregational prayer in The first issue."
"6715","(6715) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: His first prayer."
"6716","(6716) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Salah bin Zufar, he said: I prepared All the prayers are with the hudhafi, and he intercedes with the maghrib rak’ah."
"6717","(6717) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Sawda’ Al-Nadhi, who said: I prayed the Maghrib prayer, then I prayed it in A group of people. When the imam said the salutations, I stood up and performed a rak’ah of intercession, so I asked Ata’? He said: I am not sure."
"6718","(6718) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When he prays the Maghrib prayer alone, Then he prayed in congregation, interceding with his two rak’ahs."
"6719","(6719) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Hassan al-Musli narrated to us, on the authority of Bura bin Abd al-Rahman, he said: I prayed, And Ibrahim al-Nakhi and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad from Maghrib. Then we came to the mosque while they were performing the Maghrib prayer. So we entered with them and prayed. When the imam greeted, I and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad were confused, and Abraham stood up and did his intercession by praying his bow."
"6720","(6720) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Na’im, on the authority of Salah, on the authority of Hudhaifa; He prayed the noon prayer twice, the afternoon prayer twice, and the sunset prayer twice, and he made his intercession in the sunset prayer with a rak’ah."
"6721","(6721) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq; He was asked about a man who prayed Maghrib alone, then repeated it in congregation? He said: He adds a rak'ah to it."
"6722","(6722) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: He intercedes with one rak’ah. That means if he returns to Maghrib."
"6723","(6723) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Khasib bin Zaid Al-Tamimi narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan narrated to us; That a man entered the mosque while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had prayed. He said: Is there a man who will stand up to this man and pray with him? So Abu Bakr stood up and prayed with him, and he had already prayed that prayer."
"6724","(6724) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: Al-Nu’man bin Muqrin was in command of the soldiers of the people of Kufa. And Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari was with the army of the people of Basra, and I was among them, so they promised to meet with me in the morning. So one of them prayed the lunch prayer with his companions, then he came while I was praying and he prayed with you."
"6725","(6725) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Nafi’; That Ibn Omar worked on his building and prayed the noon prayer, then he passed by the Banu Awf Mosque while they were praying, so he prayed with them."
"6726","(6726) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: If a man prays in his house, then He gathered a group and prayed with them, except for sunset and dawn."
"6727","(6727) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about three people who prayed the afternoon prayer, Then they passed by a mosque, and one of them entered and prayed, and one went on, and one sat at the door? Ibn Abbas said: As for the one who prayed, his goodness increased to goodness, and as for the one who left, he went for his need, and as for the one who sat on The door is the most humiliating of them."
"6728","(6728) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I went out with Ibn Sirin, and he had prayed the Friday and afternoon prayers, so he passed by a mosque praying. It was the afternoon prayer, so he went in and prayed it with them."
"6729","(6729) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; He used to say: He should repeat all of the prayers except Maghrib, so if he fears an authority, let him pray with him, and if he finishes, let him intercede. With a blessing"
"6730","(6730) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I prayed the afternoon prayer in front of my family, then I went out with Ibn The lions, so I passed by a mosque where he was praying, and he said: Come in and let us pray. He said: I have prayed. He said: Even if you were."
"6731","(6731) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab; Concerning a man who prays the noon or afternoon prayers and then joins them in congregation. He said: I do not like for him to be exposed to them, even if It was established while he was in the mosque, so let him pray."
"6732","(6732) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, who said: I prayed the noon prayer in my house, then I came. The mosque while they were praying, so I asked Salem? He said: Pray with them."
"6733","(6733) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: The entire prayer is repeated except Maghrib, for it is an odd-numbered prayer, so do not make it a pre-emption."
"6734","(6734) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He did not dislike repeating the afternoon prayer."
"6735","(6735) Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about a man who prays the obligatory prayer, then He comes to the mosque and the people are praying that prayer? He said: He prays with them except for these two prayers. Fajr and afternoon."
"6736","(6736) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: He repeats the prayer in its entirety."
"6737","(6737) Ibn Abi Ghaniya told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam; He saw no harm in repeating the entire prayer if he did not pray it in congregation, except for the Fajr prayer. He hated repeating the Fajr prayer."
"6738","(6738) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mukhtab, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, who said: I came to Ibn Umar while he was sitting on the court. He said: And people were praying, so we said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, don’t you pray? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Do not pray a prayer twice in a day. (Abu Dawud 5800, Ahmad 19)"
"6739","(6739) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I went out with Ibn Umar from the house of Abdullah bin Khalid. Even when we looked at the door of the mosque, when the people were in the afternoon prayer, he did not remain standing until the people prayed, and he said: I prayed At home"
"6740","(6740) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Mus’ar, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of Abu Iyad: He said: Omar said: The prayer should not be repeated."
"6741","(6741) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cursed us. May God bless him and grant him peace after the dark prayer. (Ahmad 1/410, Ibn Hibban 2031)"
"6742","(6742) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Salman, meaning Ibn Rabi’ah, He said: Omar said to me: O Salman, I condemn for you the hadith narrated after the dark prayer."
"6743","(6743) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqīq, on the authority of Salman bin Rabi’ā, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab used to be harsh. We have the night prayer after the sleep prayer."
"6744","(6744) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Sulaiman ibn Mushir, on the authority of Kharsha ibn Al-Hurr, who said: I saw Omar ibn Al-Khattab He criticizes people for talking after dinner, and says: I am brown at the beginning of the night and sleepy at the end of it?"
"6745","(6745) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Misra, he said: Al-Ala bin Badr told us, on the authority of someone who heard Salman say: Beware of praying at the beginning of the night, for it is a period of time, or a departure for the end of the night, so whoever does that should pray two rak’ahs. Before he went to bed."
"6746","(6746) Abdā narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamă; They used to like it if a man prayed the Witr prayer."
"6747","(6747) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Ayyub, who said: I used to be with Sa’id bin He is cast, so I pray four rak'ahs after the evening prayer, and I speak to him, but he does not speak to me until he sleeps."
"6748","(6748) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated talking after dinner."
"6749","(6749) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Wa’il and Ibrahim, who said: A man came to Hudhayfah. He knocked on the door and Hudhayfy came out to him and said: What brings you? He said: I came to talk, and the two sides of the door opened below him. Then he said: Omar brought the sun for us after the evening prayer."
"6750","(6750) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, on the authority of Abu Barza; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade sleeping before it and talking after it. (Bukhari 771, Abu Dawud 410)"
"6751","(6751) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade sleeping before it and talking after it. (Ahmed 25. Abu Ali 4039. Abdul Razzaq 2137)"
"6752","(6752) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Omar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, spent the night at Abu Bakr’s house that night. This is the matter among the affairs of the Muslims, and I am with him. He was with him one night and I was with him."
"6753","(6753) Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Manhal, Al-Hakam, `Isa, and Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila; That Abu Laila Samar was with Ali."
"6754","(6754) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ziyad Abi Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; And Al-Miswar bin Makhramah of Samra."
"6755","(6755) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Ishaq al-Talhi, on the authority of Aisha bin Talhah; Al-Hasan bin Ali Samar is a man."
"6756","(6756) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa; That Abu Musa came to Omar bin Al-Khattab after dinner. He said: Then Omar bin Al-Khattab said to him: Why did he bring you? He said: I came to talk to you.\n He said: This is the hour? He said: He is a jurist, so Omar sat down, and they talked for a long night. I thought he said: Then Abu Musa said: Prayer, Amir. The believers? He said: We are in prayer."
"6757","(6757) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Hudhayfah and Ibn Masoud were with Al-Walid ibn Uqba."
"6758","(6758) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; He used to pray the evening prayers after the evening prayer until Aisha would say: You have arrived in the morning."
"6759","(6759) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Ibn Abbas stayed with Muawiyah until The hour of the night has passed."
"6760","(6760) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika; That a group of Quraysh were fighting, so Aisha sent to them: Go to your families, for they have I have a share in you."
"6761","(6761) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He was talking after dinner."
"6762","(6762) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm in the Samar in jurisprudence."
"6763","(6763) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah; Omar bin Abdul Aziz had a sammar."
"6764","(6764) Abu Khalid Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: Al-Qasim and his companions were sitting after dinner. They talk."
"6765","(6765) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Make your last prayer at night a Witr prayer. (Bukhari 998 and Muslim 517)"
"6766","(6746) Waki’ told us, he said: Abd al-Hamid bin Bahram told us, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Sleeping on the Witr prayer is better."
"6767","(6767) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of the Awwam, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He recommended me. My friend, may God bless him and grant him peace: I do not sleep except on the Witr prayer. (Muslim 86. Abu Dawud 1428)"
"6768","(6768) Ibn Mushir told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: My friend advised me not to sleep. Except on Witr. (Ahmed 497)"
"6769","(6769) Hushaym told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: As for me, I perform the Witr prayer. Before I sleep."
"6770","(6770) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, he said: Abu Bakr used to perform the Witr prayer. the beginning of the night, and Omar used to perform Witr at the end of the night."
"6771","(6771) Abu Muawiyah and Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever fears that he will not stand up at the end of the night, let him pray Witr at the beginning of it, and whoever hopes to stand up at the end of the night, let him pray Witr at the end of the night. His prayer at the end of the night is witnessed. Abu Muawiyah said: It is present, and that is better. (Muslim 1628, Ahmad 3/300)"
"6772","(6772) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abu Bakr: When do you perform the Witr prayer? He said: From the beginning of the night after dark, before I sleep, and he said to Omar: When do you perform the Witr prayer? He said: At the end of the night, he said to Abu Bakr: You took firmness, and he said to Omar: You took strength. (Ahmad 3/330, Abu Ali 1815)"
"6773","(6773) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he said: The Maghrib prayer is the Witr prayer of the daylight. (Nasa’i 1382. Ahmad 2/83)"
"6774","(6774) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The first time prayer was made obligatory Two rak'ahs, except for Maghrib, which is the odd-numbered prayer of the day. (Ahmad 6/241)"
"6775","(6775) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The night prayer is Witr. And the daytime prayer is Witr. Maghrib means the last of the prayers."
"6776","(6776) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I do not know that they disagree that the Maghrib is the odd number of nights. Daytime prayer"
"6777","(6777) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Maghrib is the string of fire."
"6778","(6778) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Naili, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him: The Maghrib prayer is the Witr prayer of the daytime prayer, so perform the Witr prayer of the night prayer."
"6779","(6779) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, he said: He said: Abdullah: The Witr is three times, like the Maghrib prayer and the Witr of the day."
"6780","(6780) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Majliz; He did not pray after Witr, except two rak'ahs."
"6781","(6781) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He was asked about the two rak'ahs after Witr? So he swore by God that they were an innovation."
"6782","(6782) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of his father, he said: A man from the people of Yemen asked about them for a gift? He said: Do you do them?"
"6783","(6783) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Jamra, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If you are able not to pray a prayer except You prostrated twice after that, so do it."
"6784","(6784) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyya Al-Bara’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I saw him. He prostrates two prostrations after his Witr prayer."
"6785","(6785) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Aoun bin Salih al-Bariqi narrated to us, on the authority of Atiya al-Awfi, on the authority of Abu Sa`id. The numb one; He disliked prayer after Witr."
"6786","(6786) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, who said: Because I sit after The Witr prayer and I recite is more beloved to me than the prayer after the Witr prayer."
"6787","(6787) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, He said: If you perform the Witr prayer and then stand up, recite while sitting."
"6788","(6788) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; He was asked about the two prostrations after Witr? He said: This is something that has been left behind."
"6789","(6789) Hushaym told us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to say: If a man performs the Witr prayer at the beginning of the night and then gets up at the end of the night, let him intercede and pray the Witr prayer, then To pray, then to perform Witr at the end of his prayer."
"6790","(6790) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was doing that."
"6791","(6791) Hushaym told us, he said: Al-Shaybani told us, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun; He was saying that too."
"6792","(6792) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abi Majliz; Usama bin Zayd and Ibn Abbas said: If you perform Witr prayer from the beginning of the night and then stand up to pray, pray whatever you wish and intercede, then Pray with a rak'ah."
"6793","(6793) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; He used to pray Witr at the beginning of the night, so when he stood up, he would intercede."
"6794","(6794) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan and Shu`ba narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Umayr, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Othman; He used to intercede with a rak'ah, and he would say: I only liken it to a strange camel."
"6795","(6795) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qays al-Awdi Abd al-Rahman bin Tharwan, he said: I asked Amr Ibn Maimun, on the authority of a man who performs Witr, then wakes up? He said: He intercedes with your prayer."
"6796","(6796) Mu`tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: When he prays Witr and then stands up to pray, he prays interceding after intervening."
"6797","(6797) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Kulayb Al-Jarmiy, on the authority of Saad, who said: As for me, when I prayed the Witr prayer and then stood up, I prayed two rak’ahs."
"6798","(6798) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khallas bin Amr Al-Hajri, on the authority of Ammar, who said: Either I perform Witr prayer, so when I stand up, I pray two by two, and leave the first Witr prayer as it is."
"6799","(6799) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Jamra, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and Aidh bin Amr, who said: If you perform the Witr prayer at the beginning of the night, then do not pray Witr at the end of it, and if you pray Witr at the end of it, then do not pray Witr at the beginning of it."
"6800","(6800) Hafs told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr; He used to pray Witr at the beginning of the night, and when he stood up to pray, he would pray two rak’ahs after two rak’ahs. And he was happy to do it."
"6801","(6801) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Bishr bin Harb Abi Amr, who said: I heard Rafi’ bin Khadij, He said: As for me, I perform the Witr prayer, so when I stand up, I pray two by two, and I leave the Witr prayer."
"6802","(6802) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever performs Witr prayer at the beginning of the night and then gets up, Let him pray two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs."
"6803","(6803) Hafs told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Like him"
"6804","(6804) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; Like him"
"6805","(6805) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talq ibn Muawiyah, on the authority of Alqamiyah; Did he ask him? He said: He prays two rak'ahs."
"6806","(6806) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Waqa’i, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: He prays two by two."
"6807","(6807) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Qays, who said: I met Al-Qalama and mentioned that to him, and he said: Pray two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs."
"6808","(6808) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Qais, he said: I asked Alqamiya? He said: When you prayed the Witr prayer and then stood up, perform one rak'ah until morning."
"6809","(6809) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Aisha; She was asked about the one who breaks her faith? She said: This man is playing with his string."
"6810","(6810) Hushaym told us, he said: David told us, about the people??, he said: I asked him about the one who breaks his vow? He said: We were only commanded to conclude, and we were not commanded to nullify."
"6811","(6811) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: When he performs the Witr prayer and then stands up for a night? He said: He prays intercede after intercession."
"6812","(6812) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: If a man performs Witr from the beginning night, then it seemed to him that he should pray at the end of the night, so he should pray two rak'ahs until morning."
"6813","(6813) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about the man. He performs Witr and then wakes up? He said: He prayed two by two, and they preferred that their last prayer be a Witr prayer."
"6814","(6814) Mulazim bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Badr, on the authority of Qais bin Talq, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: No, and see each other during the night. (Tirmidhi 470, Abu Dawud 1434)"
"6815","(6815) Salam bin Sulaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali (h), and Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray Witr at the time of the call to prayer, and pray The two rak'ahs with the iqamah."
"6816","(6816) Salam bin Sulaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali (h), and Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq. On the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray Witr at the time of the call to prayer, and pray the two rak’ahs with Residence"
"6817","(6817) Hushaym told us, he said: Khalid Al-Hudha’ told us, on the authority of Abu Qalab, he said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: Perhaps I performed the Witr prayer. And the imam is steadfast in the morning prayer."
"6818","(6818) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: A man came to Ibn Masoud, and he said: Witr prayer and the muezzin. He evaluates? He said: Yes, then perform Witr."
"6819","(6819) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Ibn Abbas used to pray Witr when performing the iqama."
"6820","(6820) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, he said: Abu Dhabyan told us, he said: Ali used to come out to us while we were We look at the beginning of dawn, and he says: The prayer, the best hour of Witr prayer, so when dawn comes, pray two rak’ahs. Then the prayer was performed and he prayed."
"6821","(6821) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya ibn Wathhab, on the authority of Masruq, he said: I asked Aisha on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Witr prayer all night. His beginning, his middle, and his end when he died of magic. (Tirmidhi 456. Ahmad 6/129)"
"6822","(6822) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace; Like him (Bukhari 9961 Abu Dawud 1430)"
"6823","(6823) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: I prayed with Abdullah one night All of them, so he used to raise his voice and recite the Qur’an while the people of the mosque heard him, reciting it, and did not return even when he was Before dawn comes, about the amount of time between the Maghrib call to prayer and the end of the prayer, perform the odd prayer."
"6824","(6824) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: The Witr prayer is between the two prayers."
"6825","(6825) Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I said: Which hour would I love to you, the Witr prayer? He said: When the muezzins wail."
"6826","(6826) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked Ubaydah about the man. Does he wake up when he wakes up? He said: He performs Witr."
"6827","(6827) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Bura, who said: Ibn Umar came at dawn and performed the Witr prayer."
"6828","(6828) Hushaym told us, he said: Mutarrif told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of some of Ali’s companions, he said: Ali said: Who The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Witr prayer all night; From its beginning, middle, and end, but the Witr was confirmed for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the end of the night. (Ahmed 78)"
"6829","(6829) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to pray Witr during the rest of the night, such as when he went to the Maghrib prayer."
"6830","(6830) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashīr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr ibn Sharhabeel said: Abdullah was asked about the Witr prayer after the call to prayer? He said: Yes, and after the residence."
"6831","(6831) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Hakim bin Jabir; Abu Misra was leading his people in prayer, but he slowed down for them, and he said: I was performing the Witr prayer."
"6832","(6832) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jadali, on the authority of Abu Masoud, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Witr prayer every night. From its beginning, its middle, and its end, and its end is until dawn. (Ahmad 5/272. Tabarani 681)"
"6833","(6833) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abi Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: Perform Witr before you wake up in the morning. (Musal?? 519. Ahmad 3/37)"
"6834","(6834) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to like to perform Witr at the end of the night."
"6835","(6835) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Witr prayer is performed at night, and Suhoor is performed at night."
"6836","(6836) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Witr from the beginning of the night is good. And the best is the last one."
"6837","(6837) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, They said: Witr prayer at night."
"6838","(6838) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Omar ibn Al-Khattab said: Because I like to pray the strings during the night. I have to perform the night prayer, then perform Witr prayer after the morning."
"6839","(6839) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Habib, who said: I said to Ibrahim: What is my assistant? Ali said: This is a good time for Witr. He said: With a bath before dawn."
"6840","(6840) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Harun, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: The herald of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Not to perform the Witr prayer after the break of dawn."
"6841","(6841) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Harun, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; In the same way"
"6842","(6842) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus and Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If you prayed the morning prayer and the sun rose, then The string is gone."
"6843","(6843) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah informed us, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; They both said: If you pray the morning prayer and the sun rises, do not perform Witr."
"6844","(6844) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: No Witr prayer after lunch."
"6845","(6845) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Whoever prays the morning prayer and does not perform Witr, then do not perform Witr. Aliyah"
"6846","(6846) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Whoever wakes up and does not observe Witr, is not obligated to perform Witr."
"6847","(6847) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: When dawn comes, do not perform Witr prayer. How do you make the night prayer into the day prayer?"
"6848","(6848) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of al-Hikam. He said: Perhaps the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May the peace and blessings of God be upon him like this: And he wiped his beard with his hand during prayer."
"6849","(6849) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It was said: A man should touch his beard while praying, or to leave"
"6850","(6850) Abu Bahr Al-Bakrawi narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr touching his beard while he was He prays."
"6851","(6851) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Mukhtar bin Saad, who said: I saw Al-Qasim bin Muhammad one day while he was praying. He stopped. On his beard."
"6852","(6852) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I told him: I saw Muhammad bin Sirin touching his beard while he was in Prayer? He said: I often saw him touching his beard during prayer."
"6853","(6853) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Amr ibn Hawwarith; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would probably touch his beard while he was praying. (Abu Dawud 48. Abdul Razzaq 3317)"
"6854","(6854) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of a man, who said: Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab saw a man fooling around. With his beard during prayer, he said: If this man’s heart was humble, his limbs would be humble."
"6855","(6855) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Sa`id al-Zubaidi, who said: I heard Ibrahim say: Who is in His prayer, his prayer has been spoiled."
"6856","(6856) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated to recite in prayer."
"6857","(6857) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He used to hate exhaling during prayer, and he said: It is likened to speaking."
"6858","(6858) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Do not give up your prayers, even in the middle of the day."
"6859","(6859) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Ata’, Al-Hasan, Tawoos, and Mujahid. They said: Do not leave Witr, even if the sun rises."
"6860","(6860) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, and Tawoos, that they said: He who does not perform Witr until the sun rises Flouter"
"6861","(6861) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Wabara, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man who prayed the Witr prayer in the morning and did not perform the Witr prayer? He said: What do you think, if you slept until dawn until the sun rose, wouldn’t you have been praying?"
"6862","(6862) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, who said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr, and he was asked about a man who fell asleep during the Witr prayer. Until morning? He said: He performs the Witr prayer from Al-Qabilah and two Witr prayers."
"6863","(6863) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, who said: My father performed the Witr prayer when dawn had come."
"6864","(6864) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I told him: A man goes to sleep and in the morning he prays Witr. After the morning prayer? He said: I don't know of any harm in it."
"6865","(6865) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Hammad about a man who did not perform Witr until the sun rose? He said: I prefer to pray Witr. And I asked the ruling? He said: If he wishes, he may not perform the Witr prayer."
"6866","(6866) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Karimah, on the authority of Mu’awiyah bin Qur’a, who said: A man came To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, I have not performed the Witr prayer in the morning? He said: The Witr is only performed at night. Then he said: O Messenger of God, I did not perform the Witr in the morning yet? He said: The Witr is performed only at night. Then he said: I did not perform the Witr in the morning? He said on the third or fourth: Then perform the Witr prayer. (Abdul Razzaq 4607)"
"6867","(6867) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Abd al-Malik, On the authority of Ataa, they said: If you do not do that and the dawn comes, then pray Witr, as long as you do not perform the morning prayer."
"6868","(6868) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Witr even if I realized the morning prayer."
"6869","(6869) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Nu’aym ibn Hakim, on the authority of Abu Maryam, who said: A man came to Ali and said: I slept. And you forgot the Witr until the sun rose? He said: When you wake up and remember, then pray."
"6870","(6870) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: The night prayer is two by two, so if you fear the dawn, perform the two rak’ahs Witr."
"6871","(6871) Shababah bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray Witr with one rak’ah, and he used to speak between the two rak’ahs and the last rak’ah. (Abu Dawud 1330. Ahmad 6/74)"
"6872","(6872) Hushaym told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Ibn Omar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The night prayer is twofold, the Witr prayer is one, and two prostrations before the prayer. In the morning"
"6873","(6873) Hushaym told us, saying: Yahya bin Sa’id, Ibn Aoun, and others told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; That a man asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the night prayer? He said: Two by two, so if you feel the dawn, or fear the dawn, pray a rak’ah for yourself, and your prayer will be made sufficient for you. (Bukhari 990. Muslim 145)"
"6874","(6874) Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour told us, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani; That Ibn Umar prayed two rak’ahs, then gave the salutation, then said: Bring so-and-so into my she-camel, then he got up and performed his two rak’ahs."
"6875","(6875) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Ibn Shaqiq, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The night prayer is twofold. It is two, and the string is one."
"6876","(6876) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, on the authority of his father; He used to pray Witr in a rak'ah. He said: So he was told? He said: I only kept it short."
"6877","(6877) Hushaym told us, saying: Al-Hajjaj told us about Ata’; That Mu'awiyah performed a rak'ah in the Witr prayer, but that was denied to him, so Ibn Abbas was asked? He said: He is correct in the Sunnah."
"6878","(6878) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Samar Ibn Masoud He was kept at the presence of Al-Walid bin Uqba, then they went out and fought each other, and when the morning came, each one of them bowed."
"6879","(6879) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, who said: I asked Ata’ whether he should perform the rak’ah Witr prayer? He said: Yes, if you wish."
"6880","(6880) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The family of Saad and the family of Abdullah bin Omar used to submit to Islam. Two rak'ahs of Witr, and they perform Witr with one rak'ah."
"6881","(6881) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Al-Hasan used to say the salaam in the two rak’ahs of Witr."
"6882","(6882) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id and Nafi’, who said: We saw Mu’adh the reader greeting In the two rak'ahs of Witr."
"6883","(6883) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith; That Abu Bakr performed the rak’ah Witr prayer."
"6884","(6884) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Na’ilah Ibn Farafsah said: Al-Kalbiyyah: If you kill him or call him, he used to revive the night with a rak’ah in which the Qur’an was collected, meaning: He performs Witr with it, meaning Othman, may God be pleased with him."
"6885","(6885) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ammar bin Umair, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to perform Witr with nine, but when it became sound and heavy, he performed Witr with seven. (Abu Dawud 1343. Ahmad 6/32)"
"6886","(6886) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Yahya ibn Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Umm Salama, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the Witr prayer with thirteen times, but when he grew old and weak, he prayed the Witr prayer with seven times. (Tirmidhi 457. Ahmad 322)"
"6887","(6887) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr (h) Hushaym said: And Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, they said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray the Witr prayer with nine rak’ahs, but when he became old and young, he prayed the Witr prayer with seven rak’ahs. I prayed two rak'ahs while he was sitting."
"6888","(6888) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr (h) Hushaym said: And Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, they said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to pray the Witr prayer with nine rak’ahs, but when he became old and young, he prayed the Witr prayer with seven rak’ahs. I prayed two rak'ahs while he was sitting."
"6889","(6889) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Malik ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman ibn Zayd, he said: Abdul said: God: Witr is three rak'ahs like the Maghrib prayer."
"6890","(6890) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I mentioned to Sa’id bin Jubayr what Abdullah said, The witr is seven, or five, and no less than three. Sa`id said: Ibn Abbas said: I would hate for it to be three parts. But seven, or five."
"6891","(6891) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn al-Sabbaq; Omar buried Abu Bakr at night, then he entered the mosque and prayed three times."
"6892","(6892) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, on the authority of Ismail bin Zaid, who said: Zaid bin Thabit performs the Witr prayer with five rak'ahs, without stopping during it."
"6893","(6893) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; He used to pray Witr with three rak'ahs."
"6894","(6894) Hushaym told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik bin Umayr, he said: He was Ibn Masoud prays the Witr prayer with three counts."
"6895","(6895) Hushaym told us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulaiman informed us, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahim, on the authority of Zazan Abi Omar; That Ali used to do that."
"6896","(6896) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Hayyan, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, who said: Abu Imamah used to pray Witr with three Rakat"
"6897","(6897) Abdă bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, on the authority of Uthman bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; He used to perform the Witr prayer with five rak'ahs, without stopping from them."
"6898","(6898) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Do not pray Witr with three Amputee, pray two or four rak'ahs before it."
"6899","(6899) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, who said: I heard Jabir bin Zaid saying: The string is three."
"6900","(6900) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Talq bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: The string is three."
"6901","(6901) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab; He prayed the Witr prayer with three rak'ahs, without separating between them safely."
"6902","(6902) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, he said: He told us on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymiy, he said: They used to hate that They liken the Witr prayer to the Maghrib prayer."
"6903","(6903) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to perform Witr with eleven and nine. And by seven, and by five, and it was said: There is no string with less than three."
"6904","(6904) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Muslims are unanimously agreed that the Witr prayer is three times, and the salaam is not performed except in The last of us"
"6905","(6905) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He used to perform the Witr prayer with three rak’ahs, and he would recite Qunoot in the Witr prayer before bowing."
"6906","(6906) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, on the authority of Makhoul; He used to perform the Witr prayer with three counts, not saying the salaam except in the last of them."
"6907","(6907) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: He does not say the salutation in the two rak’ahs of The string"
"6908","(6908) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, who said: Abraham forbade me to say the salaam in the two rak’ahs of Witr."
"6909","(6909) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Muslim, who said: I asked Abu Al-Aaliyah, in private, about the Witr prayer? They said: Do in it as you do in Morocco."
"6910","(6910) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas; He recited the Witr prayer with three salaams, and he did not say the salaam except in the last of them."
"6911","(6911) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: The companions of Ali and the companions of Abdullah did not submit to Islam. In the two rak'ahs of Witr."
"6912","(6912) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurārah, on the authority of Sa’d bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not say the salutation in the two rak’ahs of Witr."
"6913","(6913) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, the client of the family of Talha, on the authority of Abu Salama; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform the Witr prayer with three counts."
"6914","(6914) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Salim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Zazan; Ali used to pray the Witr prayer with three counts."
"6915","(6915) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, and Shu’bā, on the authority of Omar bin Murā, on the authority of Abi Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to perform Witr with three prayers at the end of the night, sitting."
"6916","(6916) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata bin Yazid Al-Laythi On the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: Perform the Witr prayer with five, and if you are not able, then with three. If you are not able, then with one. If you are not able, then nod. (Ahmad 418, Darmi 1582)"
"6917","(6917) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub; something like it, but he did not raise it. (Nasa’i 1402. Tahawi 291)"
"6918","(6918) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hakim, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, enacted He performed the Witr prayer, just as he did for breaking the fast and the sacrifice."
"6919","(6919) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, who said: Ali said: The Witr is not obligatory. Like the written prayer."
"6920","(6920) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Witr is Sunnah."
"6921","(6921) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muslim, a client of Abd al-Qais, who said: A man said to Ibn Umar: Have you seen the string, its Sunnah? He said: So he said: What is your age? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Witr prayer, and the Muslims performed the Witr prayer. He said: No, is it Sunnah? He said: Why, should I neglect? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Witr prayer, and the Muslims performed the Witr prayer."
"6922","(6922) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: It was said to him: Witr, What is an obligation? He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Witr prayer, and the Muslims remained steadfast in it. (Ahmad 1/120)"
"6923","(6923) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed informed us that Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban He informed him, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz al-Qurashi, that he informed him, on the authority of al-Mukhadji, a man from Banu Kinanah, that he He told him; That a man from the Ansar was in the Levant, nicknamed: Abu Muhammad, and he had female companions, and he used to say: Witr is obligatory. Al-Mukhdaji mentioned that he had gone to Ubadah ibn al-Samit and mentioned that to him, so his servants said: Abu Muhammad lied. I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Five prayers, which God has ordained for His servants. Whoever performs them will not miss He has inflicted on them something, it has come and he has a covenant with God that God will admit him to Paradise, and whoever detracts from their rights in any way, he has come but not. He has a covenant with God. If He wills, He will punish you, and if He wills, He will admit you to Paradise. (Abu Dawud 1415. Ibn Hibban 1732)"
"6924","(6924) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amer; He was asked about a man who forgot the Witr prayer? He said: It is not harmful to it, as if it were an obligation."
"6925","(6925) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not consider Witr to be obligatory."
"6926","(6926) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, and Muhammad bin Ali, who said: The sacrifice and the Witr prayer are Sunnah."
"6927","(6927) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Witr is not obligatory. But it is the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Nasa’i 1385. Ahmad 1/86)"
"6928","(6928) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rashid Al-Zufi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra Al-Zufi, on the authority of Kharijiyah bin Hudhafi Al-Adawi, who said: The Messenger of God came out against us May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: God has provided you with prayer during the night, and it is better for you than red blood. Blessings"
"6929","(6929) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, God has added a prayer to your prayer, and it is the Witr prayer. (Ahmed 2/206, Dar Qatni 3)"
"6930","(6930) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said: Witr A right or an obligation."
"6931","(6931) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It is obligatory, but it was not written down."
"6932","(6932) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Khalil ibn Murā, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Qurayh, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever does not perform Witr is not one of us. (Ahmad 2/443 Rahwayh 97)"
"6933","(6933) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: An informant informed me, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: I do not like I have abandoned Witr, even if I have reddish blessings. (Abdul Razzaq 4578)"
"6934","(6934) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, he said: Abu Al-Munib narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, on the authority of his father, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Witr is a right, so whoever does not perform the Witr is not one of us. (Abu Dawud 1414. Ahmad 5/357)"
"6935","(6935) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Indeed, God is the odd string, and He loves the string. (Bukhari 6410 and Muslim 2062)"
"6936","(6936) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah and Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, who said: The Messenger of God performed the Witr prayer. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, but not upon you. I said: to whom? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only said: “Recite Witr, O people of the Qur’an.” (Tirmidhi 453, Abu Dawud 1411)"
"6937","(6937) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Sinan Sa’id bin Sinan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O people of the Qur’an, recite the string, for God is the string and loves the string. A Bedouin said: What does the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say? He said: It is not for you, nor for your companions. (Abdul Razzaq 4571)"
"6938","(6938) Hushaym told us, he said: Juwaybir told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God is the string, and He loves the string, so perform the string, O people of the Qur’an."
"6939","(6939) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: The string is only on People of the Qur’an."
"6940","(6940) Waki` narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ammar bin Muawiyah al-Dahani, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja`d, on the authority of Hudhayfă, he said: The Witr prayer is only for the people of the Qur’an."
"6941","(6941) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It used to be said: The string is only on People of the Qur’an."
"6942","(6942) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: The Witr prayer is only for the people of the Qur’an."
"6943","(6943) Hushaym told us, saying: Abd al-Malik informed us, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, On the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in his strings: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, and {Say, O The disbelievers}, and {Say, “He is God, One.” Then when he greets, he says: Glory be to the King, the Holy, three times. (An-Nasa’i 10580. Ahmad 3/407)"
"6944","(6944) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of His father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray Witr with: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, and {Say, O disbelievers}, and {Say And God is One} And he says at the end of his prayer when he sits: Glory be to the King, the Holy, three times, extending his voice with it at the end. (Nasa’i 1430, Ahmad 3/407)"
"6945","(6945) His youth narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray Witr with: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}. (Nasa’i 1743)"
"6946","(6946) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, on the authority of Omar; He used to recite with the two Mu'awwidhatin in the Witr prayer."
"6947","(6947) Hushaym told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, he said: He was Ibn Masoud prays the Witr prayer with three rak’ahs, reciting three surahs in each rak’ah, from the end of the Mufsal, written by Abdullah."
"6948","(6948) Hushaym told us, saying: Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Zazan; Ali used to do that too."
"6949","(6949) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He used to recite in The string is in three."
"6950","(6950) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that He used to pray Witr with three things: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, {Say, O you disbelievers}, and {Say: He is God, One}."
"6951","(6951) Shababi told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray Witr with three times, reciting in them: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, and {Say, O O you disbelievers}, and {Say: He is God, One}"
"6952","(6952) Shazan narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; In the same way"
"6953","(6953) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Uthman used to recite the entire Qur’an, praying the Witr prayer. With it"
"6954","(6954) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Dinar, who said: I asked Abu Ja`far, what is recited in the two rak’ahs of Witr? He said: Nothing of the Qur’an is forbidden, so read as you wish."
"6955","(6955) Hushaym told us, saying: Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to recite in his Witr prayer at the end of his Ḍizbah."
"6956","(6956) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughiriya told us, he said: I said to Abraham: Recite in your wits from the end of my party {Amen Messenger with what was sent down to him from his Lord} until the end of the surah? He said: Yes, if you wish."
"6957","(6957) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Recite in the Witr prayer with the two Mu’awwidhatin."
"6958","(6958) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: I wished to be able to perform the Witr prayer with cows."
"6959","(6959) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhall, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Recite in the first two rak’ahs of Witr. With two surahs, and in the last: {The Messenger believed}, and {Say: He is God, One}"
"6960","(6960) Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaidah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of Ubayyah, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray Witr with: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, and {Say, O disbelievers}, and {Say And God is One}, and he says at the end of his prayer: Glory be to the King, the Holy, three times. (Abu Dawud 1418 and Ibn Hibban 2436)"
"6961","(6961) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abu Al-Hawari, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ali He said: My grandfather, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught me some words that I should say in the Qunut of Witr: O God, guide me among those whom You have guided. And protect me from whomever you have treated, and take care of me from whomever you have taken care of, and bless me in what You have given, and protect me from the evil of what you have decreed, for You are You judge, and it will not be judged against you. Indeed, he who has been in charge of you will not be humiliated. Blessed are our Lord and exalted be He. (Ibn Majah 1178 and Abu Ali 6765)"
"6962","(6962) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Harun bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to say in Qunut al-Witr: To You is praise, filling the seven heavens, filling the seven earths, and filling what is between them. Nothing more, worthy of praise and glory, it is true what the servant said, we are all your servants, there is no one who hinders what you have given, and there is no giver of what you withhold. And seriousness is of no use to someone who is serious than you."
"6963","(6963) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Saleh, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of a sheikh, nicknamed: Abu Muhammad; Al-Hussein bin Ali used to say in Qunut al-Witr: Oh God, you see and do not see, and you are in the highest view, and To You is the return, and indeed the Hereafter and the First are Yours. O God, we seek refuge in You from being humiliated and disgraced."
"6964","(6964) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Zubayr ibn Adiyy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Say in Qunut al-Witr: Oh God, we seek your help and seek your forgiveness."
"6965","(6965) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, he said: Ibn Masoud taught us to recite In Qunoot: O God, we seek Your help and seek Your forgiveness, and we praise You for what is good, and we do not disbelieve in You, and we remove and forsake those who Your dawn, O God, to You we worship, to You we pray and prostrate, to You we seek and descend, we hope for your mercy and we fear Your torment, your severe torment is attached to the disbelievers."
"6966","(6966) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is nothing temporary in Qunoot al-Witr. It is only a supplication and seeking forgiveness."
"6967","(6967) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: The traveler is not required to perform the Witr prayer."
"6968","(6968) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about Witr? He said: What do you think if I travel? He said: A rak'ah at the end of the night."
"6969","(6969) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Dinar, on the authority of a sheikh, who said: I accompanied Ibn Abbas on a journey, but I did not remember that he Stringed"
"6970","(6970) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Indeed, he performed Witr prayer during the journey."
"6971","(6971) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ibn Umar, and Ibn Abbas, who said: Witr in travel. Our age"
"6972","(6972) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Ukli, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Yazid Omar recited Qunoot in the Witr prayer before bowing."
"6973","(6973) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father; That Ali used to recite Qunoot in the Witr prayer after bowing."
"6974","(6974) Hushaym told us, saying: Ata bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman; That Ali used to recite Qunoot in the Witr prayer after bowing."
"6975","(6975) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; That Abdullah used to pray Witr and perform Qunoot before bowing."
"6976","(6976) Hushaym told us, he said: Laith told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, he said: He was the son of Masoud does not perform Qunoot in any of the prayers, except in the Witr prayer before bowing."
"6977","(6977) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of his father, who narrated it. He used to recite Qunoot in the Witr prayer before the rak’ah."
"6978","(6978) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: I made him sick and he prayed Witr prayers, so when he finished During the recitation, I bent him over to bow, but he did not do so until he recited Qunoot, then he bowed."
"6979","(6979) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad; He used to recite Qunoot in the Witr prayer before the rak’ah."
"6980","(6980) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to say: Qunoot after one has finished reciting the Qur’an."
"6981","(6981) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He used to say in Qunut al-Witr: Before Bowing when he finishes the recitation."
"6982","(6982) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He used to recite Qunoot in the Witr prayer before bowing."
"6983","(6983) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Distawai, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah; Ibn Masoud and the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the Qunoun in the Witr prayer before bowing."
"6984","(6984) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Aban bin Abi Ayash informed us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite Qunoot in the Witr prayer before bowing. He said: Then I sent his mother, Umm Abd, and she spent the night with his wives, and she told me that he had recited the Qunoot in the Witr prayer before bowing. (Daraqutni) 32. Bayhaqi 41)"
"6985","(6985) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Aban, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He recited Qunoot before bowing in the Witr prayer. (Daraqutni 5. Bayhaqi 41)"
"6986","(6986) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Awn, who said: I asked Al-Qasim about a man who performs Witr on his camel? He said: They claimed that Omar used to perform the Witr prayer on the ground."
"6987","(6987) Mu’tamir told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Omar used to perform Witr prayer on the ground."
"6988","(6988) Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr; If Ibn Umar wanted to perform the Witr prayer, he would go down and perform the Witr prayer on the ground."
"6989","(6989) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to pray on their camels and their animals. Wherever their faces were, except the obligatory prayer and the Witr prayer, they used to pray on the ground."
"6990","(6990) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: He used to pray on his camel. Wherever you go, if he wants to pray the Witr prayer, he will go down."
"6991","(6991) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Hazzaz, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: If he wanted to perform the Witr prayer, he descended Then he performed the Witr prayer."
"6992","(6992) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Harun bin Ibrahim, he said: I asked Al-Hasan, I said: Should I pray on my animal? He said: Pray for her. I said: Should you perform the Witr prayer for your animal? He said: No. Ibn Sirin said: Witr with the ground."
"6993","(6993) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He prayed on his camel, so he performed the Witr prayer on it, and said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do it. (Bukhari 1095. Ahmad 2/13)"
"6994","(6994) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Thawair, on the authority of his father; That Ali used to pray Witr on his camel."
"6995","(6995) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He performed the Witr prayer, and he said: The Witr prayer is performed on a camel."
"6996","(6996) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Omar bin Nafi’; That his father used to pray the Witr prayer for a camel."
"6997","(6997) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: Al-Hasan did not see any harm in a man performing Witr on his camel."
"6998","(6998) Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Musa ibn Uqba, who said: I accompanied Salim, but I lagged behind him. On the road, he said: What left you? He said: I said: I performed the Witr prayer. He said: Why not perform the Witr prayer on your camel?"
"6999","(6999) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; That a man asked him about a man who performs Witr and then prays? He said: He sleeps, then prays."
"7000","(7000) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated to pray Witr, then pray after praying Witr."
"7001","(7001) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Salam, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Badr; That Saad used to pray Witr, then pray."
"7002","(7002) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to like to lie between The Witr and between the two rak'ahs."
"7003","(7003) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, Hammad, and Jahm, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the one who doubts his Witr prayer, he said: He intercedes with his rak'ah and faces the Witr prayer."
"7004","(7004) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: I asked him about a man who doubts about performing the rak’ah. The string, is it facing or not? He said: No, but he should perform the rak’ah and perform two prostrations."
"7005","(7005) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to recite Qunoot only in half. It means from Ramadan."
"7006","(7006) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; In the same way"
"7007","(7007) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; He used to recite Qunoot in the middle of Ramadan."
"7008","(7008) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Ubayy led the people in disagreement with Omar, so he led them in prayer for half of Ramadan without reciting Qunoot, so when the half had passed, you recited Qunoot after bowing, so when you entered The ten people stayed and left them alone, so Muadh Al-Qaari, the reader, led them in prayer in disagreement with ‘Umar."
"7009","(7009) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Is Qunut during the month of Ramadan? He said: Omar was the first to recite the Qunoot. I said: The other half altogether? He said: Yes."
"7010","(7010) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to recite Qunoot in the middle of Ramadan."
"7011","(7011) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Muhallab bin Abi Habibi, he said: I asked Saeed bin Abi Al-Hasan about Qunoot? He said: In the middle of Ramadan, that is what we taught."
"7012","(7012) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Yahya, he said: He used to pray without even Qunoot in the Witr prayer. Half It means from Ramadan."
"7013","(7013) Azhar Al-Samman told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to say: Qunoot is in the entire Sunnah. He said: Ibn Sirin would not see him except in the middle of Ramadan."
"7014","(7014) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; That Omar ordered Ubayy to lead the people in prayer in Ramadan, and ordered him to stand alone with them for the remaining half of the six nights. ten times\n He said: Al-Hasan used to say: If there is an imam, you recite Qunoot for half the month, and if there is not an imam, you recite Qunoot for the entire month."
